## What I actually did

**New tokens in `Theme.qml`** (installed-only, nothing bundled):

```qml
readonly property string fontFamily: "Inter, Segoe UI Variable, Segoe UI, sans-serif"
readonly property string fontMono: "JetBrains Mono, Cascadia Code, Cascadia Mono, Consolas, monospace"
```

Comma-separated fallback lists, each ending in a generic — so if you don't have Inter installed, Qt silently drops to Segoe UI Variable → Segoe UI and nothing breaks. Same story for mono.

**Wired into every text-bearing component** (not just the bubble — I went through all of them):

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `Theme.qml` | `fontFamily` + `fontMono` tokens |
| `MessageBubble.qml` | body → `fontFamily`; code block + lang label → `fontMono` |
| `ChatPanel.qml` | welcome / "Say hi" / "Thinking…" → `fontFamily` |
| `LeftPanel.qml` | "Agents"/"Sessions" headers + New Session icon & label → `fontFamily` |
| `AgentRow.qml`, `SessionRow.qml` | names, titles, menu items, dialog headers, rename field → `fontFamily` |
| `Attachment.qml` | non-image label → `fontFamily` |
| `AppButton.qml`, `Main.qml` (toast) | labels → `fontFamily` |
| `InputField.qml` | **removed the `"monospace"` bug**, → `fontFamily` |

## The other bug I fixed while in there

Your message input was on `font.family: "monospace"`. That's wrong twice over — it's a *generic* name (Qt's Windows resolver guesses), and it's a monospace face for typing prose. It's now on `fontFamily`, and I pinned it to `fontMd` since it had no explicit size and was riding the OS default.

## What I did *not* do

- Didn't bundle any `.ttf` — you said installed only.
- Didn't bump `fontMd` from 14 to 15/16 for body text. I *recommended* it last message, but that changes layout metrics app-wide, so I left it as a separate decision. Say the word and it's a one-line change in the theme.
- Didn't commit. Eight files are dirty in the working tree now (`development-v2`); want me to commit each one separately with its own message, or leave it for you to eyeball in the QML live reload first?

Reload and check it — Inter should show up if you've got it installed, otherwise it's a cleaner Segoe than before. Either way, no more random monospace in your message box.
