What I touched
left_panel/LeftPanel.qml — the real fix:
agentMenu and settingsBar went from CustomRect → plain Item. The left panel is now one surfaceContainerLow card instead of four stacked copies of the same color. Their backgrounds were literally identical to the panel's, which is why you needed pink lines to see anything.
Two 1px Theme.outlineVariant divider rules — one under Agents, one above the settings bar — carry the section boundaries now. Toned regions can't do it here without killing row hover, so lines it is.
Headers normalized: both "Agents" and "Sessions" are now fontMd / DemiBold / left-aligned (was fontLg centered vs fontMd centered). Same treatment, so they read as section headers.
newSessionBtn: dropped scale: 0.9, gave it surfaceContainerHigh at rest / surfaceContainerHighest on hover, + glyph instead of the mystery bullet, left-aligned label matching the rows. It reads as a pressable row now, not a shrunken pill.
left_panel/SessionRow.qml — idle was Qt.rgba(..., 0), i.e. invisible. Now surfaceContainer at rest → surfaceContainerHigh on hover → secondaryContainer when selected. Menu/dialogs untouched.
left_panel/AgentRow.qml — same rest-state chip treatment (surfaceContainer idle, hover, selected).
generic/CustomRect.qml — debugVisible default true → false. That's a behavior change, which is why I kept it out of the earlier comment-strip commits. One-line revert if you disagree.
One thing still open: settingsBar is now a divider-topped 40px empty Item. Before it was a 96px empty CustomRect — i.e. it was always a placeholder, just a taller one. You never told me what's supposed to live there. If it's genuinely a future settings/menu holder, say so and I'll give it real content; if it's still vestigial I'd rather delete it than ship a mystery band. Your call.


