2026-10-04 20:00:27 | DEBUG    | modules.agents.models:130 | Say (full): [Agent Ame] Done. Fixed properly this time.

**What changed (10 files):**

- **`theme/Theme.qml`** — the actual root cause. `fontFamily`/`fontMono` went from comma-joined `string`s to real `var` string-lists:
  ```qml
  readonly property var fontFamily: ["Inter", "Segoe UI Variable", "Segoe UI"]
  readonly property var fontMono: ["JetBrains Mono", "Cascadia Code", "Cascadia Mono", "Consolas"]
  ```
  Dropped the `"sans-serif"`/`"monospace"` tails — those aren't real Qt family names, and Qt already falls back to the platform default on its own.
- **All 10 call sites** switched `font.family:` → `font.families:` — Main, AppButton, AgentRow, LeftPanel, SessionRow, ChatPanel, MessageBubble, InputField, Attachment.

Why it now works: `font.family` (singular) takes *one* family name and never parses a list. Handed a comma string, Qt looked for a font literally named `"Inter, Segoe UI Variable, ..."`, found nothing, and silently substituted the default — so before and after rendered identically. `font.families` (plural, Qt 6.3+) takes the list and walks it in order. Everything else in the old pass was correct wiring; only the token and the property name were wrong.

**One honest caveat, so you're not surprised again:** nothing in this repo bundles or installs Inter — there's no `addApplicationFont` call, no `res/` fonts, and the README's `utils/resource.py`/`qt_helper.py` don't actually exist. So on a machine without Inter installed, `families` correctly resolves to *Segoe UI Variable / Segoe UI* — which is already Windows' default. Visually you'd see no difference there either. If you want Inter to actually show up, it needs to be installed on the machine or shipped and loaded at startup. Want me to add that font-loading step, or are you fine with "resolves Inter if present, else OS default"?

Untouched: `CustomRect.qml` still carries the earlier `debugVisible: false` change, and `settingsBar` is still that mystery 40px band. Nothing staged or committed — your call on both.
