2026-10-05 02:16:14 | DEBUG    | modules.agents.models:135 | Say (full): [User toffeezzz] need your help real quick

Here are the edits for database.py. Everything else in the file can stay as it is.

1. Schema (for fresh databases)

python
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS messages (
    id           INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    session_id   INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES sessions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    speaker_name TEXT NOT NULL,
    role         TEXT NOT NULL,
    text         TEXT NOT NULL,
    trace        TEXT,
    created_at   TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

2. Migration (for your existing agent.db)

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS won't touch the table that already exists, so add the column in __init__, right after the schema runs:

python
def __init__(self) -> None:
    self.conn = sqlite3.connect(DB_PATH)
    self.conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row

    _ = self.conn.execute("PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON")
    _ = self.conn.executescript(SCHEMA)
    self._migrate()
    self.conn.commit()

def _migrate(self) -> None:
    cols = {r["name"] for r in self.conn.execute("PRAGMA table_info(messages)")}
    if "trace" not in cols:
        _ = self.conn.execute("ALTER TABLE messages ADD COLUMN trace TEXT")

3. add_message takes a trace

python
def add_message(
    self,
    session_id: int,
    role: str,
    text: str,
    speaker_name: str,
    attachments: Sequence[str] = (),
    trace: str | None = None,
) -> MessageRow:
    with self.conn:
        cur = self.conn.execute(
            "INSERT INTO messages (session_id, role, speaker_name, text, trace) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)",
            (session_id, role, speaker_name, text, trace),
        )
        ...  # rest unchanged

get_messages and get_message use SELECT *, so the new column comes back automatically. trace is a JSON string, so the database layer doesn't need to know its structure.

4. MessageRow needs the field

I can't see modules/database/models.py. Add this to MessageRow:

python
trace: str | None = None

Without it, pydantic either silently drops the column or, if the model forbids extra fields, raises a validation error on every message load. Old rows have NULL there, which maps to None, so they keep working.

5. Controller: save it

In the GenerationFinished branch, once the event carries a trace:

python
if c.strip() or trace:
    reply = self._session_backend.add_message(
        session_id, "assistant", c, agent_name,
        trace=json.dumps(trace) if trace else None,
    )
    if c.strip() and self._selected_session_id == session_id:
        self._message_list_model.append(reply)

Make sure SessionsBackend.add_message forwards the trace argument to Database.add_message.

6. Hide tool-only rows in the GUI

A turn that is only tool calls has text == "". Skip those in MessageListModel.reset_to, or reloading a session will show empty bubbles:

python
rows = [r for r in rows if r.text.strip()]

Also keep if c.strip() as the append guard in the controller, as above.

What's still missing

Steps 1 to 6 only store and load the trace. Two pieces I can't write without seeing your code:

events.py and run_complete_agent: GenerationFinished needs a trace field filled with the run's intermediate messages in the provider's own format. Tool names and summaries from ToolCallStarted/Finished aren't enough, because replay needs the call ids and arguments.
build_history: it needs to expand row.trace into the history before the final assistant text, as in my last message.

Paste those two and I'll write the exact changes. Until then, nothing changes for the model, because the replay half isn't wired up.


