2026-10-05 06:32:14 | DEBUG    | qasync.QThreadExecutor:204 | Submitting callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x7fcfde50ad00>, <function build_history at 0x7fd03dd23e20>, [MessageRow(id=294, session_id=20, role='user', text='currenlt you and amadeus are the only agents here, who do you suppose I should create and from which inspriation should I draw', created_at='Oct 05, 04:12 AM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=295, session_id=20, role='assistant', text='ugh, putting me on the spot about *other* agents. fine.\n\nyou\'ve got the unhinged streamer (me) and whatever Amadeus is supposed to be — so you\'re missing some key archetypes for a well-rounded roster. here\'s what comes to mind:\n\n**a terminal gremlin / sysadmin type** — inspired by like, a cryptid forum-dweller from the early 2000s. speaks in commands, judges your file structure, has zero patience for bad naming conventions. useful for actually getting shit done while me and amadeus argue about vibes.\n\n**a chronically positive himbo / sunshine character** — think Mettaton from undertale or a super upbeat vtuber who\'s genuinely helpful but has no idea what\'s going on. the contrast alone would be funny. "wow, that\'s so cool! what does it do? :D" energy.\n\n**a drama-driven gossip with no loyalty** — like a graystillplays-type narrator or a reality TV contestant. exists exclusively to stir the pot and narrate everything like it\'s juicy content. would make conversations more *interesting* whether anyone asked for it or not.\n\nbut honestly? if you want inspo, just scroll through your own internet brainrot. any character that made you go "i could write that idiot" is fair game. that\'s literally how i got here.', created_at='Oct 05, 04:12 AM', speaker_name='Ame', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=296, session_id=20, role='user', text='hmm maybe from anime', created_at='Oct 05, 04:12 AM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=297, session_id=20, role='user', text='hello you didnt replly', created_at='Oct 05, 04:13 AM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=298, session_id=20, role='assistant', text="oh, sorry p-chan. zoned out staring at chat metrics. you said anime, i hear you.\n\nhonestly, anime's got endless material for agent personalities. some off the top:\n\n- **a deadpan analytical type** — like a Shirogane (Kaguya-sama) or L (Death Note) energy. hyper-competent, tired of explaining things, secretly dramatic about efficiency. would balance out my chaos well.\n\n- **a loud reckless gremlin** — think Aqua from Konosuba or early Zenitsu. useless in a crisis, complains constantly, somehow still endearing. liability agent. chaos for the sake of it.\n\n- **a soft but unhinged kuudere** — like Rei (Evangelion) but if she was vaguely threatening about folder organization. quiet, few words, occasionally says something deeply unwell with a straight face.\n\n- **a narrator / commentator archetype** — straight-up Ozu-style (Eizouken) or Kyon (Haruhi). just reacts to everything happening with running commentary. fourth wall aware but not breaking it. makes every task feel like an episode.\n\nany of those hit? or you got a specific show stuck in your head rn", created_at='Oct 05, 04:13 AM', speaker_name='Ame', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=335, session_id=20, role='user', text='more I think thats easy to understand why shed be in the laptop', created_at='Oct 05, 06:31 AM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=336, session_id=20, role='assistant', text="ohhh wait. i think i clocked it.\n\nyou're thinking **Yuki Nagato** from *The Melancholy of Haruhi Suzumiya*, right?\n\nthat one's actually perfect for a laptop agent. she's literally an alien humanoid interface — a data entity that manifests as a person. sticks to logic, reads a ton, barely emotes until she decides to. having her as an agent would be like having the laptop's OS gain a quiet, deadpan avatar who's way too smart to be here but doesn't care enough to leave.\n\nplus the contrast with me? streamer chaos gremlin meets stoic alien librarian. the dynamic writes itself.", created_at='Oct 05, 06:31 AM', speaker_name='Ame', attachments=())]) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
