Identify any known problems or features that are not yet fully implemented.\n    Author\n    Name\n    Section', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=342, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Let me start by exploring the project structure and reading all the source files.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=343, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Now let me read all the source files. Starting with the top-level config and the main source files:\n\n', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=344, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Now let me read the GUI, server, toolkit, and agent definition files.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=345, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Now let me read the toolkit implementations and the remaining QML files for a complete picture.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=346, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Alright, I\'ve read through the entire source tree. Here\'s the comprehensive breakdown you can feed to Claude.\n\n---\n\n## Project Title\n\n**KAgent** — a multi-agent chat application with personality-driven AI characters\n\n## Project Description\n\nKAgent is a desktop application that lets you talk to multiple AI agents, each with its own distinct personality, voice, and behavior. It\'s built around the concept that an AI assistant doesn\'t have to be a bland, one-size-fits-all chatbot — you can have different "agents" for different moods or tasks, and they each remember their own conversations.\n\nThe system reads agent definitions from Markdown files with YAML frontmatter, each specifying a name, model, parameters, and a full persona prompt (with jailbreak resistance, verification keywords, etc.). It uses the OpenAI-compatible API (via OpenRouter) for LLM calls, supports image attachments and vision models, tool/function calling through a plugin-style toolkit system, and persistent SQLite storage for sessions and messages.\n\nThe GUI is built with **Qt Quick (QML)** via PyQt6 — which is an unusual and interesting choice. The UI uses a custom Material You-ish theme with smooth animations.\n\n## Project Objectives\n\n- Provide a multi-agent chat interface where each agent has a unique, persistent personality\n- Support tool-use by agents (file ops, git ops) through a pluggable toolkit/registry system\n- Persist conversations in sessions with full message history and file attachments\n- Allow runtime switching between agents and sessions\n- Handle multi-turn conversations where agents can call tools, get results, and continue\n- Support image attachments and vision-capable models\n\n## Features\n\n- **Multiple AI agents** — each with its own system prompt, model, temperature, reasoning effort, and max loop count. Defined via Markdown + YAML frontmatter files.\n- **Session-based chat** — create, rename, delete sessions. Each session stores a full message history per agent.\n- **Tool/function calling** — agents can call filesystem tools (read, write, list, move, copy, delete) and git tools (status, add, commit, diff, restore) through a dynamic toolkit registry.\n- **Image attachments** — attach images to messages, which get base64-encoded and sent to vision-capable models. Image thumbnails shown inline in chat.\n- **Code syntax highlighting** — code blocks in messages are highlighted using Pygments (Monokai theme).\n- **Thinking indicator** — animated dots and status text while the agent is generating or running tools.\n- **Hot-reload QML UI** — changes to QML files trigger automatic UI reload during development.\n- **Streaming-ready architecture** — the backend supports async iteration over agent events (GeneratingResponse → ToolCallStarted/Finished → GenerationFinished/RunError).\n- **Logging** — Rich console logging and rotating file logs with DEBUG-level detail.\n\n## Technologies Used\n\n- **Language:** Python ≥ 3.11\n- **GUI Framework:** PyQt6 with Qt Quick (QML) — `PyQt6.QtQml`, `QQmlApplicationEngine`\n- **LLM API:** OpenAI Python SDK (via OpenRouter as the provider)\n- **Database:** SQLite3 (via `sqlite3` stdlib)\n- **Other key libraries:**\n  - `pydantic` — data models and validation (AgentDefinition, MessageRow, SessionRow, LLMPayload, etc.)\n  - `python-frontmatter` + `PyYAML` — parsing agent definitions from Markdown files\n  - `Pygments` — syntax highlighting code blocks in chat\n  - `send2trash` — safe deletion (moves to OS trash instead of permanent delete)\n  - `PyMuPDF` + `pymupdf4llm` — reading PDF/DOCX documents as markdown\n  - `qasync` — Qt event loop integration with `asyncio`\n  - `python-dotenv` — loading API keys from `.env`\n  - `rich` — colored console logging\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nkagent/\n├── pyproject.toml              # Project metadata, dependencies, entry point\n├── pyrightconfig.json          # Pyright config\n├── README.md                   # This file\n├── data/\n│   └── agent.db                # SQLite database (sessions, messages, attachments)\n├── docs/\n│   └── imgs/                   # Screenshots for documentation\n├── logs/\n│   ├── app.log                 # Rotating log files\n│   ├── app.log.1\n│   └── app.log.2\n├── saves/\n│   └── config.json             # User config (username, agent settings, GUI theme, etc.)\n├── src/\n│   └── modules/\n│       ├── backend.py           # Backend protocol definitions + mock implementations\n│       ├── errors.py            # Base ProgramError\n│       ├── agents/\n│       │   ├── models.py        # BaseAgent, BasicAgent, CompleteAgent, AgentDefinition\n│       │   ├── builder.py       # Agent factory: scans definitions dir, builds agents\n│       │   ├── errors.py        # AgentError\n│       │   ├── events.py        # AgentEvent dataclasses (GeneratingResponse, etc.)\n│       │   ├── GLOBAL_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md  # Shared system prompt base for all agents\n│       │   ├── definitions/     # Agent persona definitions (Markdown + frontmatter)\n│       │   │   ├── AMADEUS.md\n│       │   │   ├── AME.md\n│       │   │   ├── AQUA.md\n│       │   │   └── SILVERWOLF.md\n│       │   └── avatars/         # Agent avatar images\n│       │       ├── amadeus.png\n│       │       ├── ame.jpg\n│       │       ├── aqua.jpg\n│       │       ├── placeholder.png\n│       │       └── silver_wolf.jpg\n│       ├── config/\n│       │   └── models.py        # (empty — config models placeholder)\n│       ├── database/\n│       │   ├── database.py      # SQLite CRUD for sessions, messages, attachments\n│       │   ├── models.py        # SessionRow, MessageRow, MemoryRow pydantic models\n│       │   └── erros.py         # DatabaseError\n│       ├── gui/\n│       │   ├── app.py           # Application entry point: sets up QApplication, engine, controller\n│       │   ├── controller.py    # AppController: bridges QML ↔ Python backends\n│       │   ├── models.py        # QAbstractListModel subclasses for agents/sessions/messages/attachments\n│       │   ├── highlighter.py   # CodeHighlighter: Pygments-based syntax highlighting for QTextDocument\n│       │   ├── loader.py        # QmlReloader: watches QML files for changes, hot-reloads UI\n│       │   └── components/      # QML UI components\n│       │       ├── Main.qml     # Root window: toast, loader, anchors\n│       │       ├── App.qml      # App layout: LeftPanel + RightPanel\n│       │       ├── generic/     # Reusable QML widgets\n│       │       │   ├── AppButton.qml\n│       │       │   ├── CustomImage.qml\n│       │       │   └── CustomRect.qml\n│       │       ├── left_panel/  # Agent list + session list\n│       │       │   ├── LeftPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── AgentRow.qml\n│       │       │   └── SessionRow.qml\n│       │       ├── right_panel/ # Chat area + input\n│       │       │   ├── RightPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── ChatPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── MessageBubble.qml\n│       │       │   ├── InputPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── InputField.qml\n│       │       │   ├── Attachment.qml\n│       │       │   └── AttachmentPreview.qml\n│       │       └── theme/\n│       │           ├── Theme.qml    # Singleton: Material You-ish color palette, spacing, fonts\n│       │           └── qmldir\n│       ├── logs/\n│       ├── server/\n│       │   ├── server.py        # Server: wraps AsyncOpenAI, handles LLM + embedding requests\n│       │   ├── models.py        # LLMPayload, LLMResponse, EmbeddingResponse, OpenRouterUsage, etc.\n│       │   └── errors.py        # ServerRequestError, LLMRequestError, EmbeddingRequestError\n│       ├── toolkits/\n│       │   ├── builder.py       # Tool/ToolKit construction from function blueprints\n│       │   ├── decorators.py    # @register_tool decorator\n│       │   ├── errors.py        # ToolKitError, ToolExecutionError\n│       │   ├── models.py        # Tool, ToolKit, ToolBlueprint, ToolCall, ToolResult dataclasses\n│       │   ├── registry.py      # ToolkitRegistry: manages active/available kits, tool execution\n│       │   ├── scanner.py       # Scans kits/ directory, builds ToolKits from SKILL.md + tools.py\n│       │   └── kits/            # Installed toolkits\n│       │       ├── file/        # Filesystem toolkit\n│       │       │   ├── SKILL.md     # Instructions for the filesystem tools (sandbox, conventions)\n│       │       │   └── tools.py     # read_file, write_file, list_dir, move_file, etc.\n│       │       └── git/         # Git operations toolkit\n│       │           ├── SKILL.md     # Instructions for git tools (order of ops, commit format)\n│       │           └── tools.py     # git_status, git_add, git_commit, git_diff, git_restore\n│       └── utils/\n│           └── logger.py        # Logging setup (Rich console + rotating file handler)\n└── tests/\n```\n\n## Installation and Setup\n\n1. **Clone the repository:**\n   ```bash\n   git clone <repo-url>\n   cd kagent\n   ```\n\n2. **Create a virtual environment** (Python ≥ 3.11):\n   ```bash\n   python -m venv .venv\n   source .venv/bin/activate   # Linux/Mac\n   # or .venv\\Scripts\\activate  # Windows\n   ```\n\n3. **Install the package and dependencies:**\n   ```bash\n   pip install -e .\n   ```\n\n4. **Set up your API key:**\n   Create a `.env` file in the project root:\n   ```\n   API_KEY=your_openrouter_api_key_here\n   ```\n   (The app uses OpenRouter as its LLM provider by default.)\n\n5. **Configure the agents (optional):**\n   Edit `saves/config.json` to set your username, default agent, model, temperature, etc.\n\n6. **Run the application:**\n   ```bash\n   kagent\n   ```\n   Or directly:\n   ```bash\n   python -m modules.gui.app\n   ```\n\n## How to Use the System\n\n1. **Launch the app.** You\'ll see a two-panel window: left panel lists agents and sessions, right panel is the chat area.\n2. **Select an agent** from the left panel. Currently available: Amadeus, Ame, Aqua, Silver Wolf.\n3. **Create a new session** by clicking the "+ New Session" button, or select an existing session.\n4. **Type your message** in the input field at the bottom right. Press Enter (Shift+Enter for newline) to send.\n5. **Attach images** by clicking the "+" button next to the input field, or drag-and-drop files.\n6. **Watch the agent respond** — you\'ll see a "Thinking…" status, then tool calls (if any), then the final reply.\n7. **Stop generation** at any time by clicking the stop (■) button.\n8. **Right-click a session** to rename or delete it.\n9. **Switch agents or sessions** at any time — each agent\'s context is isolated.\n\n## OOP Implementation\n\n### Key Classes\n\n| Class | File | Role |\n|-------|------|------|\n| `BaseAgent` (ABC) | `agents/models.py` | Abstract base for all agents. Owns the model name, system prompt, LLM params. Defines `generate()` and abstract `_build_payload()`. |\n| `BasicAgent` | `agents/models.py` | Stateless one-shot agent (system + user message, no history). Used for things like summarizers. |\n| `CompleteAgent` | `agents/models.py` | Stateful agent with message history, tool calling, and a multi-loop run cycle. The main agent type used for chat. |\n| `AgentDefinition` | `agents/models.py` | Pydantic model for agent metadata from frontmatter (name, model, params, type, etc.). |\n| `Database` | `database/database.py` | SQLite wrapper with session/message/attachment CRUD operations. |\n| `Server` | `server/server.py` | Wraps `AsyncOpenAI` client. Sends LLM and embedding requests, parses responses. |\n| `ToolkitRegistry` | `toolkits/registry.py` | Manages toolkits (core + available), tool execution, schema generation. |\n| `AppController` | `gui/controller.py` | QObject bridging QML UI and Python backends. Handles session selection, message sending, async event loop. |\n| `AgentListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` exposing agent names and avatar paths to QML ListView. |\n| `SessionListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` exposing session rows to QML ListView. |\n| `MessageListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` exposing message rows with attachment data to QML ListView. |\n| `AttachmentListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` for managing file attachments before sending. |\n| `CodeHighlighter` | `gui/highlighter.py` | Applies Pygments syntax highlighting to QTextDocument code blocks. |\n\n### Encapsulation\n\n- **`CompleteAgent`** encapsulates its own `_messages` list (conversation history) and exposes only `run()`, `generate()`, and `reset()` — external code can\'t manipulate the message list directly.\n- **`ToolkitRegistry`** encapsulates tool registration state (`_core_kits`, `_registered_kits`, `_available_kits`) and the `_tool_to_kit` lookup table. External code interacts only through `register_kit()`, `list_kits()`, `execute_tool()`, and the `schemas`/`skills` properties.\n- **`Database`** encapsulates the SQLite connection and exposes only session/message CRUD methods.\n- **`AppController`** encapsulates all async task management (`_tasks` dict), status tracking (`_status`), and backend references.\n\n### Inheritance\n\n- **`BaseAgent` → `BasicAgent`** and **`BaseAgent` → `CompleteAgent`**: Both override `_build_payload()` and `_build_user_message()` with different strategies. `CompleteAgent` adds `run()`, `_run_loop()`, `_run_tools()`, tool execution, and history management.\n- **`AgentError` → `ProgramError`**, **`DatabaseError` → `ProgramError`**: Custom exception hierarchy.\n- **`ServerRequestError` → `AgentError` → `ProgramError`**, with **`LLMRequestError`** and **`EmbeddingRequestError`** subclasses.\n- **`ToolKitError`** and **`ToolExecutionError`** extend `ProgramError`.\n\n### Polymorphism\n\n- **Backend protocols:** `SessionsBackend` and `AgentsBackend` are defined as `Protocol` classes in `backend.py`. `MockSessionBackend` and `MockAgentsBackend` implement these protocols. The `AppController` depends only on the protocols, not the concrete implementations.\n- **`BaseAgent.generate()`** is used polymorphically: `BasicAgent` and `CompleteAgent` both support it, but `CompleteAgent` adds an overloaded version that accepts `tool_choice` and `history`.\n- **`AgentEvent`** is a union type (`GeneratingResponse | GenerationFinished | ToolCallStarted | ToolCallFinished | RunError`). The controller\'s `_send()` method handles each event variant differently via pattern matching (`match event:`).\n- **Tool execution:** `ToolkitRegistry.execute_tool()` handles both async and sync tool functions transparently — async functions are awaited directly, sync functions are run in a thread executor.\n\n## Database\n\n### Database File\n`data/agent.db` — SQLite3 database.\n\n### Tables\n\n**`sessions`**\n| Column | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER PK | Auto-increment session ID |\n| `title` | TEXT NOT NULL | Session display name |\n| `agent_name` | TEXT NOT NULL | Which agent this session belongs to |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMP | Default: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP |\n\n**`messages`**\n| Column | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER PK | Auto-increment message ID |\n| `session_id` | INTEGER NOT NULL FK → sessions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `speaker_name` | TEXT NOT NULL | Who said it (user or agent name) |\n| `role` | TEXT NOT NULL | "user" or "assistant" |\n| `text` | TEXT NOT NULL | Message content |\n| `trace` | TEXT | (unused in current code) |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMP | Default: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP |\n\n**`attachments`**\n| Column | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER PK | Auto-increment |\n| `message_id` | INTEGER NOT NULL FK → messages(id) ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `path` | TEXT NOT NULL | Filesystem path to the attachment |\n\nIndexes: `idx_messages_session` on `messages(session_id, id)`, `idx_attachments_message` on `attachments(message_id)`.\n\n### Major Database Operations\n\n- **Create:** `create_session()` — INSERT into sessions. `add_message()` — INSERT into messages + INSERT into attachments (if any). Returns the created row.\n- **Read:** `get_session()`, `get_session_list()` — SELECT from sessions with optional agent_name filter, ordered by created_at DESC. `get_messages()` — SELECT from messages for a session, with attachments fetched and grouped by message_id. `get_message()` — single message with its attachments.\n- **Update:** `rename_session()` — UPDATE sessions SET title.\n- **Delete:** `delete_session()` — DELETE FROM sessions WHERE id (CASCADE deletes messages and attachments). Sessions table uses `ON DELETE CASCADE` for both messages and attachments.\n- **Search:** No free-text search — sessions are looked up by `agent_name`, messages by `session_id`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n(Found in `docs/imgs/`)\n\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `welcome_screen.png` | The initial welcome screen before any session is active |\n| `sample_chat1.png` | Example conversation with an agent |\n| `sample_chat2.png` | Another conversation example |\n| `session_rennaming.png` | The session rename dialog (right-click menu) |\n| `vision_model.png` | Chat with an image attachment being processed by a vision-capable model |\n\n## Testing\n\nThe `tests/` directory exists but is currently empty. No test files have been implemented yet. Testing is done ad-hoc through manual runs of the application.\n\n### Manual Testing Approach\n\n- **Agent loading:** Verified by running the app and checking that all 4 agents appear in the left panel.\n- **Session CRUD:** Create, select, rename (via right-click dialog), and delete sessions.\n- **Message sending:** Send a message, verify it appears in the chat, wait for agent response.\n- **Tool calling:** Send messages that trigger tool use (e.g., "list files in the current directory", "create a file called test.txt").\n- **Image attachments:** Attach images via the file picker, send, verify they appear as thumbnails in the message bubble and are included in the API request.\n- **Stop generation:** Click the stop button while an agent is generating.\n- **UI hot-reload:** Edit a QML file and verify the UI reloads automatically.\n\n## Known Issues / Limitations\n\n- **No tests** — the `tests/` directory exists but is completely empty.\n- **`trace` column unused** — messages have a `trace` TEXT column that is never written to.\n- **`config/models.py` is empty** — models intended for config validation were started but never populated.\n- **`logs/` directory has `__init__.py`-only module** — `src/modules/logs/` is an empty directory (no `__init__.py`, no files).\n- **MemoryRow** is defined in `database/models.py` but nothing in the codebase actually reads or writes to a memories table (no migration for it exists in the schema either).\n- **No remote git operations** — the git toolkit explicitly refuses push, pull, clone, fetch, branch, merge, rebase.\n- **The config file has hardcoded paths** — `saves/config.json` contains an absolute path to the old system prompt file that may not exist on other machines (`/home/toffeezzz/...`).\n- **No user authentication** — any user who launches the app gets full access.\n- **Single-user only** — there\'s no multi-user support; the username is hardcoded in `AppController.__init__` as `"toffeezzz"`.\n- **No streaming in the UI** — the Server class has a `_request_llm_streaming` method but it\'s never called from anywhere. The GUI waits for the full response.\n- **db file starts empty** — `agent.db` in the project root is 0 bytes; the real database is in `data/agent.db`.\n\n## Author\n\n**toffeezzz** — Section: N/A (not specified in source)', created_at='Oct 05, 06:42 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=())]) with args () and kwargs {} from queue
