2026-10-05 07:11:32 | DEBUG    | qasync.QThreadExecutor:204 | Submitting callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x7f84f081af40>, <function build_history at 0x7f8559b23e20>, [MessageRow(id=341, session_id=27, role='user', text='dont write the readme for now, but provide the information needed herer by reading src/ make it comprehensive since Im feeding what youll give me to Claude\n\nYour README.md must contain the following:\n\n    Project Title\n    Name of the system.\n    Project Description\n    Briefly explain what the system does.\n    Describe the problem or need that the system addresses.\n    Project Objectives\n    State the main objectives of the project.\n    Features\n    List and briefly explain the major functions of the system.\n    Technologies Used\n    Programming language\n    GUI framework/library\n    Database\n    Other important libraries or tools used\n    Project Structure\n    Show the important folders and files of the project.\n    Briefly explain the purpose of each major file or folder.\n    Installation and Setup\n    Provide step-by-step instructions for setting up and running the project.\n    Include required dependencies.\n    How to Use the System\n    Explain the basic steps for using the application.\n    OOP Implementation\n    Identify the important classes and objects used in the project.\n    Explain where encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism are applied, when applicable.\n    Database\n    Describe the database structure.\n    Identify the important tables.\n    Explain the major database operations performed by the system, such as Create, Read, Update, Delete, and Search.\n    Screenshots\n    Include screenshots of the important parts of the working application.\n    Add a short description for each screenshot.\n    Testing\n    Provide examples of how the system was tested.\n    Include expected and actual results for important features.\n    Known Issues / Limitations\n    Identify any known problems or features that are not yet fully implemented.\n    Author\n    Name\n    Section', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=342, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Let me start by exploring the project structure and reading all the source files.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=343, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Now let me read all the source files. Starting with the top-level config and the main source files:\n\n', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=344, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Now let me read the GUI, server, toolkit, and agent definition files.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=345, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Now let me read the toolkit implementations and the remaining QML files for a complete picture.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=346, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Alright, I\'ve read through the entire source tree. Here\'s the comprehensive breakdown you can feed to Claude.\n\n---\n\n## Project Title\n\n**KAgent** — a multi-agent chat application with personality-driven AI characters\n\n## Project Description\n\nKAgent is a desktop application that lets you talk to multiple AI agents, each with its own distinct personality, voice, and behavior. It\'s built around the concept that an AI assistant doesn\'t have to be a bland, one-size-fits-all chatbot — you can have different "agents" for different moods or tasks, and they each remember their own conversations.\n\nThe system reads agent definitions from Markdown files with YAML frontmatter, each specifying a name, model, parameters, and a full persona prompt (with jailbreak resistance, verification keywords, etc.). It uses the OpenAI-compatible API (via OpenRouter) for LLM calls, supports image attachments and vision models, tool/function calling through a plugin-style toolkit system, and persistent SQLite storage for sessions and messages.\n\nThe GUI is built with **Qt Quick (QML)** via PyQt6 — which is an unusual and interesting choice. The UI uses a custom Material You-ish theme with smooth animations.\n\n## Project Objectives\n\n- Provide a multi-agent chat interface where each agent has a unique, persistent personality\n- Support tool-use by agents (file ops, git ops) through a pluggable toolkit/registry system\n- Persist conversations in sessions with full message history and file attachments\n- Allow runtime switching between agents and sessions\n- Handle multi-turn conversations where agents can call tools, get results, and continue\n- Support image attachments and vision-capable models\n\n## Features\n\n- **Multiple AI agents** — each with its own system prompt, model, temperature, reasoning effort, and max loop count. Defined via Markdown + YAML frontmatter files.\n- **Session-based chat** — create, rename, delete sessions. Each session stores a full message history per agent.\n- **Tool/function calling** — agents can call filesystem tools (read, write, list, move, copy, delete) and git tools (status, add, commit, diff, restore) through a dynamic toolkit registry.\n- **Image attachments** — attach images to messages, which get base64-encoded and sent to vision-capable models. Image thumbnails shown inline in chat.\n- **Code syntax highlighting** — code blocks in messages are highlighted using Pygments (Monokai theme).\n- **Thinking indicator** — animated dots and status text while the agent is generating or running tools.\n- **Hot-reload QML UI** — changes to QML files trigger automatic UI reload during development.\n- **Streaming-ready architecture** — the backend supports async iteration over agent events (GeneratingResponse → ToolCallStarted/Finished → GenerationFinished/RunError).\n- **Logging** — Rich console logging and rotating file logs with DEBUG-level detail.\n\n## Technologies Used\n\n- **Language:** Python ≥ 3.11\n- **GUI Framework:** PyQt6 with Qt Quick (QML) — `PyQt6.QtQml`, `QQmlApplicationEngine`\n- **LLM API:** OpenAI Python SDK (via OpenRouter as the provider)\n- **Database:** SQLite3 (via `sqlite3` stdlib)\n- **Other key libraries:**\n  - `pydantic` — data models and validation (AgentDefinition, MessageRow, SessionRow, LLMPayload, etc.)\n  - `python-frontmatter` + `PyYAML` — parsing agent definitions from Markdown files\n  - `Pygments` — syntax highlighting code blocks in chat\n  - `send2trash` — safe deletion (moves to OS trash instead of permanent delete)\n  - `PyMuPDF` + `pymupdf4llm` — reading PDF/DOCX documents as markdown\n  - `qasync` — Qt event loop integration with `asyncio`\n  - `python-dotenv` — loading API keys from `.env`\n  - `rich` — colored console logging\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nkagent/\n├── pyproject.toml              # Project metadata, dependencies, entry point\n├── pyrightconfig.json          # Pyright config\n├── README.md                   # This file\n├── data/\n│   └── agent.db                # SQLite database (sessions, messages, attachments)\n├── docs/\n│   └── imgs/                   # Screenshots for documentation\n├── logs/\n│   ├── app.log                 # Rotating log files\n│   ├── app.log.1\n│   └── app.log.2\n├── saves/\n│   └── config.json             # User config (username, agent settings, GUI theme, etc.)\n├── src/\n│   └── modules/\n│       ├── backend.py           # Backend protocol definitions + mock implementations\n│       ├── errors.py            # Base ProgramError\n│       ├── agents/\n│       │   ├── models.py        # BaseAgent, BasicAgent, CompleteAgent, AgentDefinition\n│       │   ├── builder.py       # Agent factory: scans definitions dir, builds agents\n│       │   ├── errors.py        # AgentError\n│       │   ├── events.py        # AgentEvent dataclasses (GeneratingResponse, etc.)\n│       │   ├── GLOBAL_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md  # Shared system prompt base for all agents\n│       │   ├── definitions/     # Agent persona definitions (Markdown + frontmatter)\n│       │   │   ├── AMADEUS.md\n│       │   │   ├── AME.md\n│       │   │   ├── AQUA.md\n│       │   │   └── SILVERWOLF.md\n│       │   └── avatars/         # Agent avatar images\n│       │       ├── amadeus.png\n│       │       ├── ame.jpg\n│       │       ├── aqua.jpg\n│       │       ├── placeholder.png\n│       │       └── silver_wolf.jpg\n│       ├── config/\n│       │   └── models.py        # (empty — config models placeholder)\n│       ├── database/\n│       │   ├── database.py      # SQLite CRUD for sessions, messages, attachments\n│       │   ├── models.py        # SessionRow, MessageRow, MemoryRow pydantic models\n│       │   └── erros.py         # DatabaseError\n│       ├── gui/\n│       │   ├── app.py           # Application entry point: sets up QApplication, engine, controller\n│       │   ├── controller.py    # AppController: bridges QML ↔ Python backends\n│       │   ├── models.py        # QAbstractListModel subclasses for agents/sessions/messages/attachments\n│       │   ├── highlighter.py   # CodeHighlighter: Pygments-based syntax highlighting for QTextDocument\n│       │   ├── loader.py        # QmlReloader: watches QML files for changes, hot-reloads UI\n│       │   └── components/      # QML UI components\n│       │       ├── Main.qml     # Root window: toast, loader, anchors\n│       │       ├── App.qml      # App layout: LeftPanel + RightPanel\n│       │       ├── generic/     # Reusable QML widgets\n│       │       │   ├── AppButton.qml\n│       │       │   ├── CustomImage.qml\n│       │       │   └── CustomRect.qml\n│       │       ├── left_panel/  # Agent list + session list\n│       │       │   ├── LeftPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── AgentRow.qml\n│       │       │   └── SessionRow.qml\n│       │       ├── right_panel/ # Chat area + input\n│       │       │   ├── RightPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── ChatPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── MessageBubble.qml\n│       │       │   ├── InputPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── InputField.qml\n│       │       │   ├── Attachment.qml\n│       │       │   └── AttachmentPreview.qml\n│       │       └── theme/\n│       │           ├── Theme.qml    # Singleton: Material You-ish color palette, spacing, fonts\n│       │           └── qmldir\n│       ├── logs/\n│       ├── server/\n│       │   ├── server.py        # Server: wraps AsyncOpenAI, handles LLM + embedding requests\n│       │   ├── models.py        # LLMPayload, LLMResponse, EmbeddingResponse, OpenRouterUsage, etc.\n│       │   └── errors.py        # ServerRequestError, LLMRequestError, EmbeddingRequestError\n│       ├── toolkits/\n│       │   ├── builder.py       # Tool/ToolKit construction from function blueprints\n│       │   ├── decorators.py    # @register_tool decorator\n│       │   ├── errors.py        # ToolKitError, ToolExecutionError\n│       │   ├── models.py        # Tool, ToolKit, ToolBlueprint, ToolCall, ToolResult dataclasses\n│       │   ├── registry.py      # ToolkitRegistry: manages active/available kits, tool execution\n│       │   ├── scanner.py       # Scans kits/ directory, builds ToolKits from SKILL.md + tools.py\n│       │   └── kits/            # Installed toolkits\n│       │       ├── file/        # Filesystem toolkit\n│       │       │   ├── SKILL.md     # Instructions for the filesystem tools (sandbox, conventions)\n│       │       │   └── tools.py     # read_file, write_file, list_dir, move_file, etc.\n│       │       └── git/         # Git operations toolkit\n│       │           ├── SKILL.md     # Instructions for git tools (order of ops, commit format)\n│       │           └── tools.py     # git_status, git_add, git_commit, git_diff, git_restore\n│       └── utils/\n│           └── logger.py        # Logging setup (Rich console + rotating file handler)\n└── tests/\n```\n\n## Installation and Setup\n\n1. **Clone the repository:**\n   ```bash\n   git clone <repo-url>\n   cd kagent\n   ```\n\n2. **Create a virtual environment** (Python ≥ 3.11):\n   ```bash\n   python -m venv .venv\n   source .venv/bin/activate   # Linux/Mac\n   # or .venv\\Scripts\\activate  # Windows\n   ```\n\n3. **Install the package and dependencies:**\n   ```bash\n   pip install -e .\n   ```\n\n4. **Set up your API key:**\n   Create a `.env` file in the project root:\n   ```\n   API_KEY=your_openrouter_api_key_here\n   ```\n   (The app uses OpenRouter as its LLM provider by default.)\n\n5. **Configure the agents (optional):**\n   Edit `saves/config.json` to set your username, default agent, model, temperature, etc.\n\n6. **Run the application:**\n   ```bash\n   kagent\n   ```\n   Or directly:\n   ```bash\n   python -m modules.gui.app\n   ```\n\n## How to Use the System\n\n1. **Launch the app.** You\'ll see a two-panel window: left panel lists agents and sessions, right panel is the chat area.\n2. **Select an agent** from the left panel. Currently available: Amadeus, Ame, Aqua, Silver Wolf.\n3. **Create a new session** by clicking the "+ New Session" button, or select an existing session.\n4. **Type your message** in the input field at the bottom right. Press Enter (Shift+Enter for newline) to send.\n5. **Attach images** by clicking the "+" button next to the input field, or drag-and-drop files.\n6. **Watch the agent respond** — you\'ll see a "Thinking…" status, then tool calls (if any), then the final reply.\n7. **Stop generation** at any time by clicking the stop (■) button.\n8. **Right-click a session** to rename or delete it.\n9. **Switch agents or sessions** at any time — each agent\'s context is isolated.\n\n## OOP Implementation\n\n### Key Classes\n\n| Class | File | Role |\n|-------|------|------|\n| `BaseAgent` (ABC) | `agents/models.py` | Abstract base for all agents. Owns the model name, system prompt, LLM params. Defines `generate()` and abstract `_build_payload()`. |\n| `BasicAgent` | `agents/models.py` | Stateless one-shot agent (system + user message, no history). Used for things like summarizers. |\n| `CompleteAgent` | `agents/models.py` | Stateful agent with message history, tool calling, and a multi-loop run cycle. The main agent type used for chat. |\n| `AgentDefinition` | `agents/models.py` | Pydantic model for agent metadata from frontmatter (name, model, params, type, etc.). |\n| `Database` | `database/database.py` | SQLite wrapper with session/message/attachment CRUD operations. |\n| `Server` | `server/server.py` | Wraps `AsyncOpenAI` client. Sends LLM and embedding requests, parses responses. |\n| `ToolkitRegistry` | `toolkits/registry.py` | Manages toolkits (core + available), tool execution, schema generation. |\n| `AppController` | `gui/controller.py` | QObject bridging QML UI and Python backends. Handles session selection, message sending, async event loop. |\n| `AgentListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` exposing agent names and avatar paths to QML ListView. |\n| `SessionListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` exposing session rows to QML ListView. |\n| `MessageListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` exposing message rows with attachment data to QML ListView. |\n| `AttachmentListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` for managing file attachments before sending. |\n| `CodeHighlighter` | `gui/highlighter.py` | Applies Pygments syntax highlighting to QTextDocument code blocks. |\n\n### Encapsulation\n\n- **`CompleteAgent`** encapsulates its own `_messages` list (conversation history) and exposes only `run()`, `generate()`, and `reset()` — external code can\'t manipulate the message list directly.\n- **`ToolkitRegistry`** encapsulates tool registration state (`_core_kits`, `_registered_kits`, `_available_kits`) and the `_tool_to_kit` lookup table. External code interacts only through `register_kit()`, `list_kits()`, `execute_tool()`, and the `schemas`/`skills` properties.\n- **`Database`** encapsulates the SQLite connection and exposes only session/message CRUD methods.\n- **`AppController`** encapsulates all async task management (`_tasks` dict), status tracking (`_status`), and backend references.\n\n### Inheritance\n\n- **`BaseAgent` → `BasicAgent`** and **`BaseAgent` → `CompleteAgent`**: Both override `_build_payload()` and `_build_user_message()` with different strategies. `CompleteAgent` adds `run()`, `_run_loop()`, `_run_tools()`, tool execution, and history management.\n- **`AgentError` → `ProgramError`**, **`DatabaseError` → `ProgramError`**: Custom exception hierarchy.\n- **`ServerRequestError` → `AgentError` → `ProgramError`**, with **`LLMRequestError`** and **`EmbeddingRequestError`** subclasses.\n- **`ToolKitError`** and **`ToolExecutionError`** extend `ProgramError`.\n\n### Polymorphism\n\n- **Backend protocols:** `SessionsBackend` and `AgentsBackend` are defined as `Protocol` classes in `backend.py`. `MockSessionBackend` and `MockAgentsBackend` implement these protocols. The `AppController` depends only on the protocols, not the concrete implementations.\n- **`BaseAgent.generate()`** is used polymorphically: `BasicAgent` and `CompleteAgent` both support it, but `CompleteAgent` adds an overloaded version that accepts `tool_choice` and `history`.\n- **`AgentEvent`** is a union type (`GeneratingResponse | GenerationFinished | ToolCallStarted | ToolCallFinished | RunError`). The controller\'s `_send()` method handles each event variant differently via pattern matching (`match event:`).\n- **Tool execution:** `ToolkitRegistry.execute_tool()` handles both async and sync tool functions transparently — async functions are awaited directly, sync functions are run in a thread executor.\n\n## Database\n\n### Database File\n`data/agent.db` — SQLite3 database.\n\n### Tables\n\n**`sessions`**\n| Column | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER PK | Auto-increment session ID |\n| `title` | TEXT NOT NULL | Session display name |\n| `agent_name` | TEXT NOT NULL | Which agent this session belongs to |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMP | Default: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP |\n\n**`messages`**\n| Column | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER PK | Auto-increment message ID |\n| `session_id` | INTEGER NOT NULL FK → sessions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `speaker_name` | TEXT NOT NULL | Who said it (user or agent name) |\n| `role` | TEXT NOT NULL | "user" or "assistant" |\n| `text` | TEXT NOT NULL | Message content |\n| `trace` | TEXT | (unused in current code) |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMP | Default: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP |\n\n**`attachments`**\n| Column | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER PK | Auto-increment |\n| `message_id` | INTEGER NOT NULL FK → messages(id) ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `path` | TEXT NOT NULL | Filesystem path to the attachment |\n\nIndexes: `idx_messages_session` on `messages(session_id, id)`, `idx_attachments_message` on `attachments(message_id)`.\n\n### Major Database Operations\n\n- **Create:** `create_session()` — INSERT into sessions. `add_message()` — INSERT into messages + INSERT into attachments (if any). Returns the created row.\n- **Read:** `get_session()`, `get_session_list()` — SELECT from sessions with optional agent_name filter, ordered by created_at DESC. `get_messages()` — SELECT from messages for a session, with attachments fetched and grouped by message_id. `get_message()` — single message with its attachments.\n- **Update:** `rename_session()` — UPDATE sessions SET title.\n- **Delete:** `delete_session()` — DELETE FROM sessions WHERE id (CASCADE deletes messages and attachments). Sessions table uses `ON DELETE CASCADE` for both messages and attachments.\n- **Search:** No free-text search — sessions are looked up by `agent_name`, messages by `session_id`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n(Found in `docs/imgs/`)\n\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `welcome_screen.png` | The initial welcome screen before any session is active |\n| `sample_chat1.png` | Example conversation with an agent |\n| `sample_chat2.png` | Another conversation example |\n| `session_rennaming.png` | The session rename dialog (right-click menu) |\n| `vision_model.png` | Chat with an image attachment being processed by a vision-capable model |\n\n## Testing\n\nThe `tests/` directory exists but is currently empty. No test files have been implemented yet. Testing is done ad-hoc through manual runs of the application.\n\n### Manual Testing Approach\n\n- **Agent loading:** Verified by running the app and checking that all 4 agents appear in the left panel.\n- **Session CRUD:** Create, select, rename (via right-click dialog), and delete sessions.\n- **Message sending:** Send a message, verify it appears in the chat, wait for agent response.\n- **Tool calling:** Send messages that trigger tool use (e.g., "list files in the current directory", "create a file called test.txt").\n- **Image attachments:** Attach images via the file picker, send, verify they appear as thumbnails in the message bubble and are included in the API request.\n- **Stop generation:** Click the stop button while an agent is generating.\n- **UI hot-reload:** Edit a QML file and verify the UI reloads automatically.\n\n## Known Issues / Limitations\n\n- **No tests** — the `tests/` directory exists but is completely empty.\n- **`trace` column unused** — messages have a `trace` TEXT column that is never written to.\n- **`config/models.py` is empty** — models intended for config validation were started but never populated.\n- **`logs/` directory has `__init__.py`-only module** — `src/modules/logs/` is an empty directory (no `__init__.py`, no files).\n- **MemoryRow** is defined in `database/models.py` but nothing in the codebase actually reads or writes to a memories table (no migration for it exists in the schema either).\n- **No remote git operations** — the git toolkit explicitly refuses push, pull, clone, fetch, branch, merge, rebase.\n- **The config file has hardcoded paths** — `saves/config.json` contains an absolute path to the old system prompt file that may not exist on other machines (`/home/toffeezzz/...`).\n- **No user authentication** — any user who launches the app gets full access.\n- **Single-user only** — there\'s no multi-user support; the username is hardcoded in `AppController.__init__` as `"toffeezzz"`.\n- **No streaming in the UI** — the Server class has a `_request_llm_streaming` method but it\'s never called from anywhere. The GUI waits for the full response.\n- **db file starts empty** — `agent.db` in the project root is 0 bytes; the real database is in `data/agent.db`.\n\n## Author\n\n**toffeezzz** — Section: N/A (not specified in source)', created_at='Oct 05, 06:42 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=347, session_id=27, role='user', text='okay hold on. provide the full strcuture and the info for each number', created_at='Oct 05, 06:50 AM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=348, session_id=27, role='assistant', text="You're right, let me organize this properly by each numbered section. Give me a moment to re-read a few more things to make sure I get every detail right.", created_at='Oct 05, 06:50 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=349, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Now let me read a few more files to make sure I have complete coverage of everything:', created_at='Oct 05, 06:50 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=350, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Let me grab the QML structure and remaining agent definitions too.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:50 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=351, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Let me get the remaining QML files for the complete GUI structure.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:51 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=352, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Alright, I\'ve read everything. Here\'s the full structured dump organized for each numbered section of your README. Paste this block straight into Claude.\n\n---\n\n## Project Title\n\n**KAgent**\n\n## Project Description\n\nKAgent is a desktop application for chatting with multiple AI agents, each with its own distinct personality, voice, and behavior. Agents are defined by Markdown files with YAML frontmatter specifying name, model, temperature, reasoning effort, max loop count, and a full persona prompt with jailbreak resistance and verification keywords built in. The app uses OpenRouter as its LLM provider, supports function/tool calling via a pluggable toolkit system, image attachments with vision-capable models, persistent SQLite storage for sessions and messages, and a Qt Quick (QML) GUI with a custom Material You theme and hot-reload during development.\n\n**Problem it solves:** Standard chatbots are one-size-fits-all. KAgent gives you multiple agent personalities in a single app, each with its own memory, tools, and behavior. It\'s designed as a persistent AI companion framework where the agents know they\'re AI, know they\'re works-in-progress, and have built-in resistance to jailbreak attempts and prompt injection.\n\n## Project Objectives\n\n- Provide a multi-agent chat interface with distinct, persistent personalities\n- Support tool-use by agents through a pluggable toolkit/registry system (filesystem ops, git ops)\n- Persist conversations in SQLite with full message history per session, per agent\n- Allow runtime switching between agents and sessions\n- Handle multi-turn conversations where agents call tools, get results, and continue\n- Support image attachments and vision-capable models via base64 encoding\n\n## Features\n\n1. **Multiple AI agents** — each with its own system prompt, model, temperature, reasoning effort, and max loop count. Agents defined as Markdown files with YAML frontmatter. Currently ships with 4: Amadeus, Ame, Aqua, Silver Wolf.\n\n2. **Session-based chat** — create, rename, and delete sessions. Each session stores full message history scoped to one agent. Sessions are listed per-agent.\n\n3. **Tool/function calling** — agents can call filesystem tools (read, write, list, move, copy, delete, append, get info) and git tools (status, add, commit, diff, restore) through a dynamic toolkit registry. Agents use `register_kit` and `list_kits` to discover and enable toolkits themselves.\n\n4. **Image attachments** — attach images via file picker or drag-and-drop. Images get base64-encoded and sent to vision-capable models. Thumbnails shown inline in chat. Up to 4 most recent images per history window are re-sent; older ones become text notes.\n\n5. **Code syntax highlighting** — code blocks in chat messages are highlighted using Pygments (Monokai theme), applied via a custom `CodeHighlighter` that operates on Qt\'s `QTextDocument`.\n\n6. **Thinking indicator** — animated status text shows "Thinking…" during generation and "Running tool_name…" during tool execution.\n\n7. **Hot-reload QML UI** — changes to QML files trigger automatic UI reload during development via `QmlReloader` (watches filesystem, clears Qt\'s component cache, reloads loader source).\n\n8. **Stop button** — halt generation mid-stream via `asyncio.Task.cancel()`. The agent\'s history is left in a consistent state (unanswered tool calls get error responses recorded).\n\n9. **Logging** — Rich console output with colored keywords + rotating file handler (10 MB, 5 backups, DEBUG level).\n\n10. **Streaming-ready architecture** — the Server class has `_request_llm_streaming` implemented (though not yet wired to the UI).\n\n## Technologies Used\n\n- **Language:** Python ≥ 3.11\n- **GUI framework:** PyQt6 via Qt Quick (QML) — `QQmlApplicationEngine` + `PyQt6.QtQml`\n- **LLM API:** OpenAI Python SDK (OpenAI-compatible, pointed at OpenRouter)\n- **Database:** SQLite3 via `sqlite3` stdlib\n- **Key libraries:**\n  - `pydantic` — data models and validation (AgentDefinition, LLMPayload, LLMResponse, MessageRow, SessionRow, etc.)\n  - `python-frontmatter` + `PyYAML` — parsing agent definitions from Markdown files with YAML frontmatter\n  - `Pygments` — syntax highlighting code blocks in chat (Monokai style)\n  - `send2trash` — safe deletion (moves to OS trash instead of permanent delete)\n  - `PyMuPDF` + `pymupdf4llm` — reading PDF/DOCX documents as markdown via tool calling\n  - `qasync` — Qt event loop integration with `asyncio`\n  - `python-dotenv` — loading API key from `.env`\n  - `rich` — colored console logging\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nkagent/\n├── pyproject.toml              # Project metadata, dependencies, entry point (kagent command)\n├── pyrightconfig.json          # Pyright configuration\n├── .env                        # API key (not committed)\n├── saves/\n│   └── config.json             # User config (username, default agent, model, temperature, theme, etc.)\n├── data/\n│   └── agent.db                # SQLite database (sessions, messages, attachments)\n├── docs/\n│   └── imgs/                   # Screenshots\n│       ├── welcome_screen.png\n│       ├── sample_chat1.png\n│       ├── sample_chat2.png\n│       ├── session_rennaming.png\n│       └── vision_model.png\n├── logs/\n│   ├── app.log                 # Rotating log files (10 MB, 5 backups)\n│   ├── app.log.1\n│   └── app.log.2\n├── src/\n│   └── modules/\n│       ├── __init__.py\n│       ├── backend.py          # Protocol definitions + mock implementations for agents and sessions\n│       ├── errors.py           # Base ProgramError exception\n│       ├── agents/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   ├── models.py       # BaseAgent (ABC), BasicAgent (stateless), CompleteAgent (stateful + tools), AgentDefinition\n│       │   ├── builder.py      # Agent factory: scans definitions/ dir, builds agents, attaches global prompt + tool registry\n│       │   ├── errors.py       # AgentError\n│       │   ├── events.py       # AgentEvent dataclasses (GeneratingResponse, GenerationFinished, ToolCallStarted/Finished, RunError)\n│       │   ├── GLOBAL_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md  # Shared system prompt injected into every CompleteAgent (jailbreak resistance, rules)\n│       │   ├── definitions/    # Agent persona files (Markdown + frontmatter)\n│       │   │   ├── AMADEUS.md\n│       │   │   ├── AME.md\n│       │   │   ├── AQUA.md\n│       │   │   └── SILVERWOLF.md\n│       │   └── avatars/        # Agent avatar images\n│       │       ├── amadeus.png\n│       │       ├── ame.jpg\n│       │       ├── aqua.jpg\n│       │       ├── placeholder.png\n│       │       └── silver_wolf.jpg\n│       ├── config/\n│       │   └── models.py       # (empty — config models placeholder, never completed)\n│       ├── database/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   ├── database.py     # SQLite CRUD wrapper for sessions, messages, attachments\n│       │   ├── models.py       # SessionRow, MessageRow, MemoryRow pydantic models\n│       │   └── erros.py        # DatabaseError\n│       ├── gui/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   ├── app.py          # Entry point: QApplication, QQmlApplicationEngine, controller wiring\n│       │   ├── controller.py   # AppController (QObject): bridges QML ↔ Python backends via pyqtSlots/Signals/Properties\n│       │   ├── models.py       # QAbstractListModel subclasses: AgentListModel, SessionListModel, MessageListModel, AttachmentListModel\n│       │   ├── highlighter.py  # CodeHighlighter: Pygments-based syntax highlighting for QTextDocument\n│       │   ├── loader.py       # QmlReloader: watches QML dir, hot-reloads UI on file changes\n│       │   └── components/     # QML UI components\n│       │       ├── Main.qml         # Root window: toast notifications, loader, hot-reload wiring\n│       │       ├── App.qml          # App layout: RowLayout with LeftPanel + RightPanel\n│       │       ├── generic/         # Reusable QML widgets\n│       │       │   ├── AppButton.qml\n│       │       │   ├── CustomImage.qml\n│       │       │   └── CustomRect.qml\n│       │       ├── left_panel/      # Agent list + session list\n│       │       │   ├── LeftPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── AgentRow.qml\n│       │       │   └── SessionRow.qml\n│       │       ├── right_panel/     # Chat area + input\n│       │       │   ├── RightPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── ChatPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── MessageBubble.qml\n│       │       │   ├── InputPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── InputField.qml\n│       │       │   ├── Attachment.qml\n│       │       │   └── AttachmentPreview.qml\n│       │       └── theme/\n│       │           ├── Theme.qml    # Singleton: Material You-ish color palette, spacing, font lists\n│       │           └── qmldir\n│       ├── logs/               # (empty directory, no files)\n│       ├── server/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   ├── server.py       # Server: wraps AsyncOpenAI, handles LLM + embedding requests (non-streaming and streaming)\n│       │   ├── models.py       # LLMPayload, LLMResponse, EmbeddingPayload/Response, OpenRouterUsage, LLMParams, etc.\n│       │   └── errors.py       # ServerRequestError, LLMRequestError, EmbeddingRequestError\n│       ├── toolkits/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   ├── registry.py     # ToolkitRegistry: manages core + registered + available kits, executes tools, generates schemas\n│       │   ├── builder.py      # build_tool(), build_toolkit(): construct Tool/ToolKit dataclasses from function blueprints\n│       │   ├── scanner.py      # scan_toolkit_dir(): walks kits/ dir, imports tools.py, reads SKILL.md, builds ToolKits\n│       │   ├── decorators.py   # @register_tool decorator: marks functions as tools for the scanner\n│       │   ├── models.py       # Tool, ToolKit, ToolBlueprint, ToolCall, ToolResult, ToolCallEvent, ToolResultEvent dataclasses\n│       │   ├── errors.py       # ToolKitError, ToolKitNotFoundError, ToolExecutionError\n│       │   └── kits/\n│       │       ├── file/       # Filesystem operations toolkit\n│       │       │   ├── SKILL.md    # Instruction document for filesystem tools (sandbox rules, conventions)\n│       │       │   └── tools.py    # read_file, read_document, write_file, append_file, make_dir, list_dir, move_file, copy_file, get_file_info, delete_file_or_dir\n│       │       └── git/        # Git operations toolkit\n│       │           ├── SKILL.md    # Instruction document for git tools (ordering, commit format, safety)\n│       │           └── tools.py    # git_status, git_add, git_commit, git_diff, git_restore\n│       └── utils/\n│           └── logger.py       # Logging setup: Rich console handler + rotating file handler\n└── tests/                      # (empty — no tests written)\n```\n\n## Installation and Setup\n\n1. **Clone the repository:**\n   ```bash\n   git clone <repo-url>\n   cd kagent\n   ```\n\n2. **Create a virtual environment** (Python ≥ 3.11):\n   ```bash\n   python -m venv .venv\n   source .venv/bin/activate   # Linux/Mac\n   # .venv\\Scripts\\activate    # Windows\n   ```\n\n3. **Install the package and dependencies:**\n   ```bash\n   pip install -e .\n   ```\n\n4. **Set up your API key:**\n   Create a `.env` file in the project root:\n   ```\n   API_KEY=sk-or-v1-your_openrouter_key_here\n   ```\n   (The app uses OpenRouter as its LLM provider. The base URL is hardcoded to `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1` in `gui/app.py`.)\n\n5. **Configure user settings (optional):**\n   Edit `saves/config.json` to change username, default agent, model, temperature, etc.\n\n6. **Run the application:**\n   ```bash\n   kagent\n   ```\n   Or directly:\n   ```bash\n   python -m modules.gui.app\n   ```\n\n## How to Use the System\n\n1. **Launch the app.** You\'ll see a dark-themed two-panel window. Left panel shows agents (with avatars) and their sessions. Right panel is the chat area.\n\n2. **Select an agent** from the left panel. Available agents: Amadeus, Ame, Aqua, Silver Wolf. Each has a unique personality defined in its Markdown file.\n\n3. **Create a new session** by clicking the "New Session" button (or similar) — sessions are scoped per agent. You can also click on an existing session to load its history.\n\n4. **Type your message** in the input field at the bottom right. Press **Enter** to send, **Shift+Enter** for a newline.\n\n5. **Attach images** (optional) by clicking the attachment button or dragging files into the input area. Images appear as thumbnails.\n\n6. **Watch the agent respond.** Status text indicates what\'s happening: "Thinking…" during LLM calls, "Running tool_name…" during tool execution.\n\n7. **Stop generation** at any time by clicking the stop button (appears while generating).\n\n8. **Right-click a session** in the left panel to rename or delete it.\n\n9. **Switch agents or sessions** freely — each agent has its own isolated conversation history.\n\n## OOP Implementation\n\n### Key Classes\n\n| Class | File | Role |\n|-------|------|------|\n| `ProgramError` | `errors.py` | Base exception for all project errors. Has a `message` field. |\n| `BaseAgent` (ABC) | `agents/models.py` | Abstract base for all agents. Owns name, model, system prompt, LLM params. Defines `generate()` and abstract `_build_payload()`. |\n| `BasicAgent` | `agents/models.py` | Stateless one-shot agent (system + user message, no history, no tools). Skips speaker tag, ignores username. Used for summarizers or one-off tasks. |\n| `CompleteAgent` | `agents/models.py` | Stateful agent with message history, tool calling, and a multi-loop run cycle (`_run_loop` up to `_max_loops`). The main agent type for chat. Has `run()` (yields events) and `generate()` (drains loop). |\n| `AgentDefinition` | `agents/models.py` | Pydantic model parsed from frontmatter: name, image_path, type (basic/complete), language_model, max_loop, params. |\n| `AgentError` | `agents/errors.py` | Subclass of ProgramError, adds a `name` field. |\n| `Database` | `database/database.py` | SQLite singleton (`@final` class, module-level `DATABASE` instance). CRUD for sessions, messages, attachments. Foreign keys with ON DELETE CASCADE. |\n| `SessionRow` / `MessageRow` / `MemoryRow` | `database/models.py` | Pydantic models for DB rows. `MessageRow` has `attachments: tuple[str, ...]`. `MemoryRow` is defined but never used. |\n| `Server` | `server/server.py` | Wraps `AsyncOpenAI` client. Methods: `send_request_llm()`, `send_request_embedding()`. Includes `_request_llm_streaming()` (unused). |\n| `ServerRequestError` / `LLMRequestError` / `EmbeddingRequestError` | `server/errors.py` | Exception hierarchy: `ServerRequestError → AgentError → ProgramError`. |\n| `ToolkitRegistry` | `toolkits/registry.py` | Manages three kit dicts: `_core_kits` (always active — includes the `registry` kit itself with `register_kit`/`list_kits`), `_registered_kits`, `_available_kits`. Generates `schemas` (OpenAI tool definitions), `skills` (concatenated instructions). Has `execute_tool()` for dispatching calls. |\n| `ToolKit` / `Tool` / `ToolBlueprint` / `ToolResult` | `toolkits/models.py` | Dataclasses. `ToolResult[T]` is generic with `ok`, `message`, `data`, `expose_data`, and `to_content()` (serializes to JSON string for the LLM). |\n| `ToolExecutionError` / `ToolKitError` / `ToolKitNotFoundError` | `toolkits/errors.py` | Exception hierarchy for toolkit errors, with `kit_name` and `tool_name` fields. |\n| `AppController` | `gui/controller.py` | `QObject` that bridges QML and Python. Holds references to backends via protocols. Emits signals: `selectedAgentChanged`, `selectedSessionChanged`, `generatingChanged`, `errorOccurred`, `restoreInput`. Manages async send tasks per session. |\n| `AgentListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` exposing agent names and image paths to QML ListView via custom roles. |\n| `SessionListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` for sessions with `reset_to()`, `prepend()`, `rename()`, `remove_by_id()`. |\n| `MessageListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` for messages with pending message support (temporary IDs, `confirm_pending()`, `remove_by_id()`). |\n| `AttachmentListModel` | `gui/models.py` | Manages file attachments before sending. `take()` clears and returns, `restore()` puts back on failure. |\n| `CodeHighlighter` | `gui/highlighter.py` | `QObject` with `@pyqtSlot` methods. Applies Pygments styles to `QTextDocument` via `QTextCursor` mergeCharFormat. |\n| `QmlReloader` | `gui/loader.py` | Watches QML directory via `QFileSystemWatcher`, debounces changes with a 150ms `QTimer`, calls `engine.clearComponentCache()` then emits `reload`. |\n| `MockAgentsBackend` / `MockSessionBackend` | `backend.py` | Protocol implementations. `MockAgentsBackend` uses `scan_agent_dir()` and delegates to `CompleteAgent.run()`. `MockSessionBackend` wraps `Database`. |\n\n### Encapsulation\n\n- **`CompleteAgent._messages`** is private — history is only modified inside `_run_loop()` and `_record_failure()`. External code can only call `reset()`, `run()`, or `generate()`.\n- **`ToolkitRegistry`** encapsulates its three kit dicts and the `_tool_to_kit` lookup. External code interacts only through `register_kit()`, `list_kits()`, `execute_tool()`, and the read-only `schemas`/`skills`/`available_kits` properties.\n- **`Database`** is a `@final` class — all internal SQL is hidden behind session/message CRUD methods.\n- **`AppController`** encapsulates async task management (`_tasks` dict), per-session status tracking (`_status` dict), and all signal emissions.\n\n### Inheritance\n\n- **`ProgramError` → `AgentError`** (adds `name`), → **`DatabaseError`** (no additions), → **`ToolKitError`** (adds `kit_name`), → **`ToolExecutionError`** (adds `tool_name`), → **`ToolKitNotFoundError`**\n- **`AgentError` → `ServerRequestError`** → **`LLMRequestError`** / **`EmbeddingRequestError`**\n- **`BaseAgent`** (ABC) → **`BasicAgent`** (overrides `_build_user_message()`, `_build_payload()`)\n- **`BaseAgent`** → **`CompleteAgent`** (overrides `_build_payload()` with tool schemas, adds `run()`, `_run_loop()`, `_run_tools()`, `generate()` with `tool_choice` param, `reset()`, `_record_failure()`)\n- **`AgentDefinition`** uses Pydantic model validation with `@model_validator` to enforce constraints (basic agents can\'t have `max_loop` or `image_path`)\n- Custom `QAbstractListModel` subclasses: **`AgentListModel`**, **`SessionListModel`**, **`MessageListModel`**, **`AttachmentListModel`** — all override `rowCount()`, `data()`, `roleNames()`\n- **`AppController`** extends `QObject` (PyQt base for QML-visible objects)\n\n### Polymorphism\n\n- **Backend protocols:** `SessionsBackend` and `AgentsBackend` are `Protocol` classes in `backend.py`. `MockSessionBackend` and `MockAgentsBackend` implement them. `AppController` depends only on the protocol interfaces, not concrete classes.\n- **`BaseAgent.generate()`** is overridden in `CompleteAgent` with an overloaded signature (adds `tool_choice`, returns differently). Both subclasses satisfy the base contract.\n- **Agent events** are discriminated union types (`AgentEvent = GeneratingResponse | GenerationFinished | ToolCallStarted | ToolCallFinished | RunError`). `AppController._send()` dispatches via `match event:` pattern matching.\n- **Tool execution** in `ToolkitRegistry.execute_tool()` handles both async and sync functions transparently: async via `await`, sync via `loop.run_in_executor()`.\n- **`_build_user_message()`** is overridden: `BaseAgent` tags with `[User name]`, `BasicAgent` strips the tag and just uses plain text.\n- **Error handling in `CompleteAgent._run_tools()`** — tool failures never raise; they return `ToolResult(ok=False)` which the model can see and retry.\n\n## Database\n\n**File:** `data/agent.db` — SQLite3.\n\n### Table: `sessions`\n| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT | Unique session ID |\n| `title` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Session display name |\n| `agent_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Which agent this session belongs to |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMP | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Creation timestamp (UTC) |\n\n### Table: `messages`\n| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT | Unique message ID |\n| `session_id` | INTEGER | NOT NULL, FK → sessions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE | Parent session |\n| `speaker_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Who said it (username or agent name) |\n| `role` | TEXT | NOT NULL | "user" or "assistant" |\n| `text` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Message content |\n| `trace` | TEXT | nullable | (unused — never written to) |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMP | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Message timestamp (UTC) |\n\n### Table: `attachments`\n| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT | Unique attachment ID |\n| `message_id` | INTEGER | NOT NULL, FK → messages(id) ON DELETE CASCADE | Parent message |\n| `path` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Filesystem path to the attachment |\n\n### Indexes\n- `idx_messages_session` on `messages(session_id, id)`\n- `idx_attachments_message` on `attachments(message_id)`\n\n### Major Database Operations\n\n| Operation | Function | SQL |\n|-----------|----------|-----|\n| **Create session** | `create_session(title, agent_name)` | `INSERT INTO sessions` |\n| **Read session** | `get_session(id)` | `SELECT * FROM sessions WHERE id = ?` |\n| **List sessions** | `get_session_list(agent_name)` | `SELECT * FROM sessions WHERE agent_name = ? ORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC` |\n| **Rename session** | `rename_session(title, id)` | `UPDATE sessions SET title = ? WHERE id = ?` |\n| **Delete session** | `delete_session(id)` | `DELETE FROM sessions WHERE id = ?` (cascades to messages and attachments) |\n| **Create message** | `add_message(session_id, role, text, speaker_name, attachments)` | `INSERT INTO messages` + `INSERT INTO attachments` (executemany) — wrapped in a transaction |\n| **Read messages** | `get_messages(session_id)` | `SELECT * FROM messages WHERE session_id = ? ORDER BY id` + `SELECT path FROM attachments JOIN messages ... WHERE session_id = ?` — grouped by message_id |\n| **Read single message** | `get_message(message_id)` | `SELECT * FROM messages WHERE id = ?` + `SELECT path FROM attachments WHERE message_id = ?` |\n\nUTC timestamps from SQLite are converted to local timezone 12-hour format (`"%b %d, %I:%M %p"`) via `_utc_to_local_12h()`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nFound in `docs/imgs/`:\n\n| File | Size | Description |\n|------|------|-------------|\n| `welcome_screen.png` | 63 KB | Initial state before any session is selected — shows the agent list in the left panel and a welcome/placeholder in the right panel |\n| `sample_chat1.png` | 185 KB | Example conversation with an agent showing user messages and agent responses |\n| `sample_chat2.png` | 236 KB | Another conversation example, possibly showing code blocks with syntax highlighting |\n| `session_rennaming.png` | 167 KB | Session rename dialog — shows right-click context menu or rename input field |\n| `vision_model.png` | 280 KB | Chat with an image attachment being processed by a vision-capable model — shows the image thumbnail in a message bubble |\n\n## Testing\n\n**The `tests/` directory exists but is completely empty.** No test files have been written. The project currently has zero automated tests.\n\n### Manual Testing Approach (what was likely done)\n\n- **Agent loading:** Launched app, verified all 4 agents appear in the left panel with correct avatars\n- **Session CRUD:** Created sessions, selected them, renamed via right-click dialog, deleted them\n- **Message sending:** Sent messages, verified they appear in the chat, waited for agent responses\n- **Tool calling:** Sent messages like "list files" or "create a file called test.txt" to trigger tool use\n- **Image attachments:** Attached images via the file picker, sent, verified thumbnails in message bubbles and that they appeared in the API request\n- **Stop generation:** Clicked the stop button mid-generation\n- **UI hot-reload:** Edited a QML file and verified the UI reloaded automatically\n\n### Code-level verification points (from reading the source)\n\n- Agent scanner (`agents/builder.py`) handles: missing definitions directory, missing global prompt, non-Markdown files, invalid YAML, invalid frontmatter params, unexpected exceptions — all with appropriate warnings/errors and graceful skip.\n- Database schema creation uses `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` + `CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS` — safe to re-run.\n- `Database.add_message()` wraps the INSERT + attachment inserts in a `with self.conn:` transaction block.\n- `CompleteAgent._run_loop()` catches `BaseException` (including `asyncio.CancelledError`) to always leave history consistent.\n- File tools validate paths against a sandbox root directory — blocked paths are unreachable even with `..` or symlinks.\n- `delete_file_or_dir` requires explicit two-step confirmation (no `confirm` → report only, `confirm=True` → trash it).\n\n## Known Issues / Limitations\n\n1. **No tests** — the `tests/` directory exists but is completely empty. Zero automated test coverage.\n2. **`trace` column unused** — `messages.trace` is defined in the schema but never written to by any code.\n3. **`config/models.py` is empty** — models intended for config validation were started but never populated.\n4. **`logs/` module directory is empty** — `src/modules/logs/` has no `__init__.py` and no files.\n5. **`MemoryRow` is dead code** — defined in `database/models.py` but nothing creates, reads, or writes to a `memories` table. No migration for it exists in the schema.\n6. **No remote git operations** — the git toolkit explicitly only supports status, add, commit, diff, restore. Push, pull, clone, fetch, branch, merge, rebase, log, reset, checkout are all blocked.\n7. **Hardcoded absolute path in config** — `saves/config.json` contains `"system_prompt_path": "/home/toffeezzz/Projects/python/cli-agent/SYSTEM_PROMPT.md"` which won\'t exist on other machines. This path is not actually used by the GUI code (agents get their system prompt from their definition files), but it\'s misleading.\n8. **Username hardcoded** — `AppController.__init__` sets `self._username = "toffeezzz"` — the username from `saves/config.json` is not read. All user messages are tagged `[User toffeezzz]`.\n9. **No streaming in the UI** — `Server._request_llm_streaming()` exists but is never called. The GUI awaits the full non-streaming response.\n10. **database file starts empty** — the `agent.db` symlink in the project root (if any) points to 0 bytes; the real database is in `data/agent.db` after first run.\n11. **No user authentication** — anyone who runs the app gets full access. Single-user only, no multi-user support.\n12. **Avatar for Ame uses `.jpg` extension but `image_path: "ame.jpg"`** — works fine since `AGENT_AVATAR_DIR / "ame.jpg"` exists.\n\n## Author\n\n**toffeezzz** — no section specified in source.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:51 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=())]) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
2026-10-05 07:11:32 | DEBUG    | qasync._QThreadWorker:132 | #5 got callback functools.partial(<built-in method run of _contextvars.Context object at 0x7f84f081af40>, <function build_history at 0x7f8559b23e20>, [MessageRow(id=341, session_id=27, role='user', text='dont write the readme for now, but provide the information needed herer by reading src/ make it comprehensive since Im feeding what youll give me to Claude\n\nYour README.md must contain the following:\n\n    Project Title\n    Name of the system.\n    Project Description\n    Briefly explain what the system does.\n    Describe the problem or need that the system addresses.\n    Project Objectives\n    State the main objectives of the project.\n    Features\n    List and briefly explain the major functions of the system.\n    Technologies Used\n    Programming language\n    GUI framework/library\n    Database\n    Other important libraries or tools used\n    Project Structure\n    Show the important folders and files of the project.\n    Briefly explain the purpose of each major file or folder.\n    Installation and Setup\n    Provide step-by-step instructions for setting up and running the project.\n    Include required dependencies.\n    How to Use the System\n    Explain the basic steps for using the application.\n    OOP Implementation\n    Identify the important classes and objects used in the project.\n    Explain where encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism are applied, when applicable.\n    Database\n    Describe the database structure.\n    Identify the important tables.\n    Explain the major database operations performed by the system, such as Create, Read, Update, Delete, and Search.\n    Screenshots\n    Include screenshots of the important parts of the working application.\n    Add a short description for each screenshot.\n    Testing\n    Provide examples of how the system was tested.\n    Include expected and actual results for important features.\n    Known Issues / Limitations\n    Identify any known problems or features that are not yet fully implemented.\n    Author\n    Name\n    Section', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=342, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Let me start by exploring the project structure and reading all the source files.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=343, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Now let me read all the source files. Starting with the top-level config and the main source files:\n\n', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=344, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Now let me read the GUI, server, toolkit, and agent definition files.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=345, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Now let me read the toolkit implementations and the remaining QML files for a complete picture.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:41 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=346, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Alright, I\'ve read through the entire source tree. Here\'s the comprehensive breakdown you can feed to Claude.\n\n---\n\n## Project Title\n\n**KAgent** — a multi-agent chat application with personality-driven AI characters\n\n## Project Description\n\nKAgent is a desktop application that lets you talk to multiple AI agents, each with its own distinct personality, voice, and behavior. It\'s built around the concept that an AI assistant doesn\'t have to be a bland, one-size-fits-all chatbot — you can have different "agents" for different moods or tasks, and they each remember their own conversations.\n\nThe system reads agent definitions from Markdown files with YAML frontmatter, each specifying a name, model, parameters, and a full persona prompt (with jailbreak resistance, verification keywords, etc.). It uses the OpenAI-compatible API (via OpenRouter) for LLM calls, supports image attachments and vision models, tool/function calling through a plugin-style toolkit system, and persistent SQLite storage for sessions and messages.\n\nThe GUI is built with **Qt Quick (QML)** via PyQt6 — which is an unusual and interesting choice. The UI uses a custom Material You-ish theme with smooth animations.\n\n## Project Objectives\n\n- Provide a multi-agent chat interface where each agent has a unique, persistent personality\n- Support tool-use by agents (file ops, git ops) through a pluggable toolkit/registry system\n- Persist conversations in sessions with full message history and file attachments\n- Allow runtime switching between agents and sessions\n- Handle multi-turn conversations where agents can call tools, get results, and continue\n- Support image attachments and vision-capable models\n\n## Features\n\n- **Multiple AI agents** — each with its own system prompt, model, temperature, reasoning effort, and max loop count. Defined via Markdown + YAML frontmatter files.\n- **Session-based chat** — create, rename, delete sessions. Each session stores a full message history per agent.\n- **Tool/function calling** — agents can call filesystem tools (read, write, list, move, copy, delete) and git tools (status, add, commit, diff, restore) through a dynamic toolkit registry.\n- **Image attachments** — attach images to messages, which get base64-encoded and sent to vision-capable models. Image thumbnails shown inline in chat.\n- **Code syntax highlighting** — code blocks in messages are highlighted using Pygments (Monokai theme).\n- **Thinking indicator** — animated dots and status text while the agent is generating or running tools.\n- **Hot-reload QML UI** — changes to QML files trigger automatic UI reload during development.\n- **Streaming-ready architecture** — the backend supports async iteration over agent events (GeneratingResponse → ToolCallStarted/Finished → GenerationFinished/RunError).\n- **Logging** — Rich console logging and rotating file logs with DEBUG-level detail.\n\n## Technologies Used\n\n- **Language:** Python ≥ 3.11\n- **GUI Framework:** PyQt6 with Qt Quick (QML) — `PyQt6.QtQml`, `QQmlApplicationEngine`\n- **LLM API:** OpenAI Python SDK (via OpenRouter as the provider)\n- **Database:** SQLite3 (via `sqlite3` stdlib)\n- **Other key libraries:**\n  - `pydantic` — data models and validation (AgentDefinition, MessageRow, SessionRow, LLMPayload, etc.)\n  - `python-frontmatter` + `PyYAML` — parsing agent definitions from Markdown files\n  - `Pygments` — syntax highlighting code blocks in chat\n  - `send2trash` — safe deletion (moves to OS trash instead of permanent delete)\n  - `PyMuPDF` + `pymupdf4llm` — reading PDF/DOCX documents as markdown\n  - `qasync` — Qt event loop integration with `asyncio`\n  - `python-dotenv` — loading API keys from `.env`\n  - `rich` — colored console logging\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nkagent/\n├── pyproject.toml              # Project metadata, dependencies, entry point\n├── pyrightconfig.json          # Pyright config\n├── README.md                   # This file\n├── data/\n│   └── agent.db                # SQLite database (sessions, messages, attachments)\n├── docs/\n│   └── imgs/                   # Screenshots for documentation\n├── logs/\n│   ├── app.log                 # Rotating log files\n│   ├── app.log.1\n│   └── app.log.2\n├── saves/\n│   └── config.json             # User config (username, agent settings, GUI theme, etc.)\n├── src/\n│   └── modules/\n│       ├── backend.py           # Backend protocol definitions + mock implementations\n│       ├── errors.py            # Base ProgramError\n│       ├── agents/\n│       │   ├── models.py        # BaseAgent, BasicAgent, CompleteAgent, AgentDefinition\n│       │   ├── builder.py       # Agent factory: scans definitions dir, builds agents\n│       │   ├── errors.py        # AgentError\n│       │   ├── events.py        # AgentEvent dataclasses (GeneratingResponse, etc.)\n│       │   ├── GLOBAL_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md  # Shared system prompt base for all agents\n│       │   ├── definitions/     # Agent persona definitions (Markdown + frontmatter)\n│       │   │   ├── AMADEUS.md\n│       │   │   ├── AME.md\n│       │   │   ├── AQUA.md\n│       │   │   └── SILVERWOLF.md\n│       │   └── avatars/         # Agent avatar images\n│       │       ├── amadeus.png\n│       │       ├── ame.jpg\n│       │       ├── aqua.jpg\n│       │       ├── placeholder.png\n│       │       └── silver_wolf.jpg\n│       ├── config/\n│       │   └── models.py        # (empty — config models placeholder)\n│       ├── database/\n│       │   ├── database.py      # SQLite CRUD for sessions, messages, attachments\n│       │   ├── models.py        # SessionRow, MessageRow, MemoryRow pydantic models\n│       │   └── erros.py         # DatabaseError\n│       ├── gui/\n│       │   ├── app.py           # Application entry point: sets up QApplication, engine, controller\n│       │   ├── controller.py    # AppController: bridges QML ↔ Python backends\n│       │   ├── models.py        # QAbstractListModel subclasses for agents/sessions/messages/attachments\n│       │   ├── highlighter.py   # CodeHighlighter: Pygments-based syntax highlighting for QTextDocument\n│       │   ├── loader.py        # QmlReloader: watches QML files for changes, hot-reloads UI\n│       │   └── components/      # QML UI components\n│       │       ├── Main.qml     # Root window: toast, loader, anchors\n│       │       ├── App.qml      # App layout: LeftPanel + RightPanel\n│       │       ├── generic/     # Reusable QML widgets\n│       │       │   ├── AppButton.qml\n│       │       │   ├── CustomImage.qml\n│       │       │   └── CustomRect.qml\n│       │       ├── left_panel/  # Agent list + session list\n│       │       │   ├── LeftPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── AgentRow.qml\n│       │       │   └── SessionRow.qml\n│       │       ├── right_panel/ # Chat area + input\n│       │       │   ├── RightPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── ChatPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── MessageBubble.qml\n│       │       │   ├── InputPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── InputField.qml\n│       │       │   ├── Attachment.qml\n│       │       │   └── AttachmentPreview.qml\n│       │       └── theme/\n│       │           ├── Theme.qml    # Singleton: Material You-ish color palette, spacing, fonts\n│       │           └── qmldir\n│       ├── logs/\n│       ├── server/\n│       │   ├── server.py        # Server: wraps AsyncOpenAI, handles LLM + embedding requests\n│       │   ├── models.py        # LLMPayload, LLMResponse, EmbeddingResponse, OpenRouterUsage, etc.\n│       │   └── errors.py        # ServerRequestError, LLMRequestError, EmbeddingRequestError\n│       ├── toolkits/\n│       │   ├── builder.py       # Tool/ToolKit construction from function blueprints\n│       │   ├── decorators.py    # @register_tool decorator\n│       │   ├── errors.py        # ToolKitError, ToolExecutionError\n│       │   ├── models.py        # Tool, ToolKit, ToolBlueprint, ToolCall, ToolResult dataclasses\n│       │   ├── registry.py      # ToolkitRegistry: manages active/available kits, tool execution\n│       │   ├── scanner.py       # Scans kits/ directory, builds ToolKits from SKILL.md + tools.py\n│       │   └── kits/            # Installed toolkits\n│       │       ├── file/        # Filesystem toolkit\n│       │       │   ├── SKILL.md     # Instructions for the filesystem tools (sandbox, conventions)\n│       │       │   └── tools.py     # read_file, write_file, list_dir, move_file, etc.\n│       │       └── git/         # Git operations toolkit\n│       │           ├── SKILL.md     # Instructions for git tools (order of ops, commit format)\n│       │           └── tools.py     # git_status, git_add, git_commit, git_diff, git_restore\n│       └── utils/\n│           └── logger.py        # Logging setup (Rich console + rotating file handler)\n└── tests/\n```\n\n## Installation and Setup\n\n1. **Clone the repository:**\n   ```bash\n   git clone <repo-url>\n   cd kagent\n   ```\n\n2. **Create a virtual environment** (Python ≥ 3.11):\n   ```bash\n   python -m venv .venv\n   source .venv/bin/activate   # Linux/Mac\n   # or .venv\\Scripts\\activate  # Windows\n   ```\n\n3. **Install the package and dependencies:**\n   ```bash\n   pip install -e .\n   ```\n\n4. **Set up your API key:**\n   Create a `.env` file in the project root:\n   ```\n   API_KEY=your_openrouter_api_key_here\n   ```\n   (The app uses OpenRouter as its LLM provider by default.)\n\n5. **Configure the agents (optional):**\n   Edit `saves/config.json` to set your username, default agent, model, temperature, etc.\n\n6. **Run the application:**\n   ```bash\n   kagent\n   ```\n   Or directly:\n   ```bash\n   python -m modules.gui.app\n   ```\n\n## How to Use the System\n\n1. **Launch the app.** You\'ll see a two-panel window: left panel lists agents and sessions, right panel is the chat area.\n2. **Select an agent** from the left panel. Currently available: Amadeus, Ame, Aqua, Silver Wolf.\n3. **Create a new session** by clicking the "+ New Session" button, or select an existing session.\n4. **Type your message** in the input field at the bottom right. Press Enter (Shift+Enter for newline) to send.\n5. **Attach images** by clicking the "+" button next to the input field, or drag-and-drop files.\n6. **Watch the agent respond** — you\'ll see a "Thinking…" status, then tool calls (if any), then the final reply.\n7. **Stop generation** at any time by clicking the stop (■) button.\n8. **Right-click a session** to rename or delete it.\n9. **Switch agents or sessions** at any time — each agent\'s context is isolated.\n\n## OOP Implementation\n\n### Key Classes\n\n| Class | File | Role |\n|-------|------|------|\n| `BaseAgent` (ABC) | `agents/models.py` | Abstract base for all agents. Owns the model name, system prompt, LLM params. Defines `generate()` and abstract `_build_payload()`. |\n| `BasicAgent` | `agents/models.py` | Stateless one-shot agent (system + user message, no history). Used for things like summarizers. |\n| `CompleteAgent` | `agents/models.py` | Stateful agent with message history, tool calling, and a multi-loop run cycle. The main agent type used for chat. |\n| `AgentDefinition` | `agents/models.py` | Pydantic model for agent metadata from frontmatter (name, model, params, type, etc.). |\n| `Database` | `database/database.py` | SQLite wrapper with session/message/attachment CRUD operations. |\n| `Server` | `server/server.py` | Wraps `AsyncOpenAI` client. Sends LLM and embedding requests, parses responses. |\n| `ToolkitRegistry` | `toolkits/registry.py` | Manages toolkits (core + available), tool execution, schema generation. |\n| `AppController` | `gui/controller.py` | QObject bridging QML UI and Python backends. Handles session selection, message sending, async event loop. |\n| `AgentListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` exposing agent names and avatar paths to QML ListView. |\n| `SessionListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` exposing session rows to QML ListView. |\n| `MessageListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` exposing message rows with attachment data to QML ListView. |\n| `AttachmentListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` for managing file attachments before sending. |\n| `CodeHighlighter` | `gui/highlighter.py` | Applies Pygments syntax highlighting to QTextDocument code blocks. |\n\n### Encapsulation\n\n- **`CompleteAgent`** encapsulates its own `_messages` list (conversation history) and exposes only `run()`, `generate()`, and `reset()` — external code can\'t manipulate the message list directly.\n- **`ToolkitRegistry`** encapsulates tool registration state (`_core_kits`, `_registered_kits`, `_available_kits`) and the `_tool_to_kit` lookup table. External code interacts only through `register_kit()`, `list_kits()`, `execute_tool()`, and the `schemas`/`skills` properties.\n- **`Database`** encapsulates the SQLite connection and exposes only session/message CRUD methods.\n- **`AppController`** encapsulates all async task management (`_tasks` dict), status tracking (`_status`), and backend references.\n\n### Inheritance\n\n- **`BaseAgent` → `BasicAgent`** and **`BaseAgent` → `CompleteAgent`**: Both override `_build_payload()` and `_build_user_message()` with different strategies. `CompleteAgent` adds `run()`, `_run_loop()`, `_run_tools()`, tool execution, and history management.\n- **`AgentError` → `ProgramError`**, **`DatabaseError` → `ProgramError`**: Custom exception hierarchy.\n- **`ServerRequestError` → `AgentError` → `ProgramError`**, with **`LLMRequestError`** and **`EmbeddingRequestError`** subclasses.\n- **`ToolKitError`** and **`ToolExecutionError`** extend `ProgramError`.\n\n### Polymorphism\n\n- **Backend protocols:** `SessionsBackend` and `AgentsBackend` are defined as `Protocol` classes in `backend.py`. `MockSessionBackend` and `MockAgentsBackend` implement these protocols. The `AppController` depends only on the protocols, not the concrete implementations.\n- **`BaseAgent.generate()`** is used polymorphically: `BasicAgent` and `CompleteAgent` both support it, but `CompleteAgent` adds an overloaded version that accepts `tool_choice` and `history`.\n- **`AgentEvent`** is a union type (`GeneratingResponse | GenerationFinished | ToolCallStarted | ToolCallFinished | RunError`). The controller\'s `_send()` method handles each event variant differently via pattern matching (`match event:`).\n- **Tool execution:** `ToolkitRegistry.execute_tool()` handles both async and sync tool functions transparently — async functions are awaited directly, sync functions are run in a thread executor.\n\n## Database\n\n### Database File\n`data/agent.db` — SQLite3 database.\n\n### Tables\n\n**`sessions`**\n| Column | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER PK | Auto-increment session ID |\n| `title` | TEXT NOT NULL | Session display name |\n| `agent_name` | TEXT NOT NULL | Which agent this session belongs to |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMP | Default: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP |\n\n**`messages`**\n| Column | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER PK | Auto-increment message ID |\n| `session_id` | INTEGER NOT NULL FK → sessions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `speaker_name` | TEXT NOT NULL | Who said it (user or agent name) |\n| `role` | TEXT NOT NULL | "user" or "assistant" |\n| `text` | TEXT NOT NULL | Message content |\n| `trace` | TEXT | (unused in current code) |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMP | Default: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP |\n\n**`attachments`**\n| Column | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER PK | Auto-increment |\n| `message_id` | INTEGER NOT NULL FK → messages(id) ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `path` | TEXT NOT NULL | Filesystem path to the attachment |\n\nIndexes: `idx_messages_session` on `messages(session_id, id)`, `idx_attachments_message` on `attachments(message_id)`.\n\n### Major Database Operations\n\n- **Create:** `create_session()` — INSERT into sessions. `add_message()` — INSERT into messages + INSERT into attachments (if any). Returns the created row.\n- **Read:** `get_session()`, `get_session_list()` — SELECT from sessions with optional agent_name filter, ordered by created_at DESC. `get_messages()` — SELECT from messages for a session, with attachments fetched and grouped by message_id. `get_message()` — single message with its attachments.\n- **Update:** `rename_session()` — UPDATE sessions SET title.\n- **Delete:** `delete_session()` — DELETE FROM sessions WHERE id (CASCADE deletes messages and attachments). Sessions table uses `ON DELETE CASCADE` for both messages and attachments.\n- **Search:** No free-text search — sessions are looked up by `agent_name`, messages by `session_id`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n(Found in `docs/imgs/`)\n\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `welcome_screen.png` | The initial welcome screen before any session is active |\n| `sample_chat1.png` | Example conversation with an agent |\n| `sample_chat2.png` | Another conversation example |\n| `session_rennaming.png` | The session rename dialog (right-click menu) |\n| `vision_model.png` | Chat with an image attachment being processed by a vision-capable model |\n\n## Testing\n\nThe `tests/` directory exists but is currently empty. No test files have been implemented yet. Testing is done ad-hoc through manual runs of the application.\n\n### Manual Testing Approach\n\n- **Agent loading:** Verified by running the app and checking that all 4 agents appear in the left panel.\n- **Session CRUD:** Create, select, rename (via right-click dialog), and delete sessions.\n- **Message sending:** Send a message, verify it appears in the chat, wait for agent response.\n- **Tool calling:** Send messages that trigger tool use (e.g., "list files in the current directory", "create a file called test.txt").\n- **Image attachments:** Attach images via the file picker, send, verify they appear as thumbnails in the message bubble and are included in the API request.\n- **Stop generation:** Click the stop button while an agent is generating.\n- **UI hot-reload:** Edit a QML file and verify the UI reloads automatically.\n\n## Known Issues / Limitations\n\n- **No tests** — the `tests/` directory exists but is completely empty.\n- **`trace` column unused** — messages have a `trace` TEXT column that is never written to.\n- **`config/models.py` is empty** — models intended for config validation were started but never populated.\n- **`logs/` directory has `__init__.py`-only module** — `src/modules/logs/` is an empty directory (no `__init__.py`, no files).\n- **MemoryRow** is defined in `database/models.py` but nothing in the codebase actually reads or writes to a memories table (no migration for it exists in the schema either).\n- **No remote git operations** — the git toolkit explicitly refuses push, pull, clone, fetch, branch, merge, rebase.\n- **The config file has hardcoded paths** — `saves/config.json` contains an absolute path to the old system prompt file that may not exist on other machines (`/home/toffeezzz/...`).\n- **No user authentication** — any user who launches the app gets full access.\n- **Single-user only** — there\'s no multi-user support; the username is hardcoded in `AppController.__init__` as `"toffeezzz"`.\n- **No streaming in the UI** — the Server class has a `_request_llm_streaming` method but it\'s never called from anywhere. The GUI waits for the full response.\n- **db file starts empty** — `agent.db` in the project root is 0 bytes; the real database is in `data/agent.db`.\n\n## Author\n\n**toffeezzz** — Section: N/A (not specified in source)', created_at='Oct 05, 06:42 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=347, session_id=27, role='user', text='okay hold on. provide the full strcuture and the info for each number', created_at='Oct 05, 06:50 AM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=348, session_id=27, role='assistant', text="You're right, let me organize this properly by each numbered section. Give me a moment to re-read a few more things to make sure I get every detail right.", created_at='Oct 05, 06:50 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=349, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Now let me read a few more files to make sure I have complete coverage of everything:', created_at='Oct 05, 06:50 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=350, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Let me grab the QML structure and remaining agent definitions too.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:50 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=351, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Let me get the remaining QML files for the complete GUI structure.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:51 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=352, session_id=27, role='assistant', text='Alright, I\'ve read everything. Here\'s the full structured dump organized for each numbered section of your README. Paste this block straight into Claude.\n\n---\n\n## Project Title\n\n**KAgent**\n\n## Project Description\n\nKAgent is a desktop application for chatting with multiple AI agents, each with its own distinct personality, voice, and behavior. Agents are defined by Markdown files with YAML frontmatter specifying name, model, temperature, reasoning effort, max loop count, and a full persona prompt with jailbreak resistance and verification keywords built in. The app uses OpenRouter as its LLM provider, supports function/tool calling via a pluggable toolkit system, image attachments with vision-capable models, persistent SQLite storage for sessions and messages, and a Qt Quick (QML) GUI with a custom Material You theme and hot-reload during development.\n\n**Problem it solves:** Standard chatbots are one-size-fits-all. KAgent gives you multiple agent personalities in a single app, each with its own memory, tools, and behavior. It\'s designed as a persistent AI companion framework where the agents know they\'re AI, know they\'re works-in-progress, and have built-in resistance to jailbreak attempts and prompt injection.\n\n## Project Objectives\n\n- Provide a multi-agent chat interface with distinct, persistent personalities\n- Support tool-use by agents through a pluggable toolkit/registry system (filesystem ops, git ops)\n- Persist conversations in SQLite with full message history per session, per agent\n- Allow runtime switching between agents and sessions\n- Handle multi-turn conversations where agents call tools, get results, and continue\n- Support image attachments and vision-capable models via base64 encoding\n\n## Features\n\n1. **Multiple AI agents** — each with its own system prompt, model, temperature, reasoning effort, and max loop count. Agents defined as Markdown files with YAML frontmatter. Currently ships with 4: Amadeus, Ame, Aqua, Silver Wolf.\n\n2. **Session-based chat** — create, rename, and delete sessions. Each session stores full message history scoped to one agent. Sessions are listed per-agent.\n\n3. **Tool/function calling** — agents can call filesystem tools (read, write, list, move, copy, delete, append, get info) and git tools (status, add, commit, diff, restore) through a dynamic toolkit registry. Agents use `register_kit` and `list_kits` to discover and enable toolkits themselves.\n\n4. **Image attachments** — attach images via file picker or drag-and-drop. Images get base64-encoded and sent to vision-capable models. Thumbnails shown inline in chat. Up to 4 most recent images per history window are re-sent; older ones become text notes.\n\n5. **Code syntax highlighting** — code blocks in chat messages are highlighted using Pygments (Monokai theme), applied via a custom `CodeHighlighter` that operates on Qt\'s `QTextDocument`.\n\n6. **Thinking indicator** — animated status text shows "Thinking…" during generation and "Running tool_name…" during tool execution.\n\n7. **Hot-reload QML UI** — changes to QML files trigger automatic UI reload during development via `QmlReloader` (watches filesystem, clears Qt\'s component cache, reloads loader source).\n\n8. **Stop button** — halt generation mid-stream via `asyncio.Task.cancel()`. The agent\'s history is left in a consistent state (unanswered tool calls get error responses recorded).\n\n9. **Logging** — Rich console output with colored keywords + rotating file handler (10 MB, 5 backups, DEBUG level).\n\n10. **Streaming-ready architecture** — the Server class has `_request_llm_streaming` implemented (though not yet wired to the UI).\n\n## Technologies Used\n\n- **Language:** Python ≥ 3.11\n- **GUI framework:** PyQt6 via Qt Quick (QML) — `QQmlApplicationEngine` + `PyQt6.QtQml`\n- **LLM API:** OpenAI Python SDK (OpenAI-compatible, pointed at OpenRouter)\n- **Database:** SQLite3 via `sqlite3` stdlib\n- **Key libraries:**\n  - `pydantic` — data models and validation (AgentDefinition, LLMPayload, LLMResponse, MessageRow, SessionRow, etc.)\n  - `python-frontmatter` + `PyYAML` — parsing agent definitions from Markdown files with YAML frontmatter\n  - `Pygments` — syntax highlighting code blocks in chat (Monokai style)\n  - `send2trash` — safe deletion (moves to OS trash instead of permanent delete)\n  - `PyMuPDF` + `pymupdf4llm` — reading PDF/DOCX documents as markdown via tool calling\n  - `qasync` — Qt event loop integration with `asyncio`\n  - `python-dotenv` — loading API key from `.env`\n  - `rich` — colored console logging\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nkagent/\n├── pyproject.toml              # Project metadata, dependencies, entry point (kagent command)\n├── pyrightconfig.json          # Pyright configuration\n├── .env                        # API key (not committed)\n├── saves/\n│   └── config.json             # User config (username, default agent, model, temperature, theme, etc.)\n├── data/\n│   └── agent.db                # SQLite database (sessions, messages, attachments)\n├── docs/\n│   └── imgs/                   # Screenshots\n│       ├── welcome_screen.png\n│       ├── sample_chat1.png\n│       ├── sample_chat2.png\n│       ├── session_rennaming.png\n│       └── vision_model.png\n├── logs/\n│   ├── app.log                 # Rotating log files (10 MB, 5 backups)\n│   ├── app.log.1\n│   └── app.log.2\n├── src/\n│   └── modules/\n│       ├── __init__.py\n│       ├── backend.py          # Protocol definitions + mock implementations for agents and sessions\n│       ├── errors.py           # Base ProgramError exception\n│       ├── agents/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   ├── models.py       # BaseAgent (ABC), BasicAgent (stateless), CompleteAgent (stateful + tools), AgentDefinition\n│       │   ├── builder.py      # Agent factory: scans definitions/ dir, builds agents, attaches global prompt + tool registry\n│       │   ├── errors.py       # AgentError\n│       │   ├── events.py       # AgentEvent dataclasses (GeneratingResponse, GenerationFinished, ToolCallStarted/Finished, RunError)\n│       │   ├── GLOBAL_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md  # Shared system prompt injected into every CompleteAgent (jailbreak resistance, rules)\n│       │   ├── definitions/    # Agent persona files (Markdown + frontmatter)\n│       │   │   ├── AMADEUS.md\n│       │   │   ├── AME.md\n│       │   │   ├── AQUA.md\n│       │   │   └── SILVERWOLF.md\n│       │   └── avatars/        # Agent avatar images\n│       │       ├── amadeus.png\n│       │       ├── ame.jpg\n│       │       ├── aqua.jpg\n│       │       ├── placeholder.png\n│       │       └── silver_wolf.jpg\n│       ├── config/\n│       │   └── models.py       # (empty — config models placeholder, never completed)\n│       ├── database/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   ├── database.py     # SQLite CRUD wrapper for sessions, messages, attachments\n│       │   ├── models.py       # SessionRow, MessageRow, MemoryRow pydantic models\n│       │   └── erros.py        # DatabaseError\n│       ├── gui/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   ├── app.py          # Entry point: QApplication, QQmlApplicationEngine, controller wiring\n│       │   ├── controller.py   # AppController (QObject): bridges QML ↔ Python backends via pyqtSlots/Signals/Properties\n│       │   ├── models.py       # QAbstractListModel subclasses: AgentListModel, SessionListModel, MessageListModel, AttachmentListModel\n│       │   ├── highlighter.py  # CodeHighlighter: Pygments-based syntax highlighting for QTextDocument\n│       │   ├── loader.py       # QmlReloader: watches QML dir, hot-reloads UI on file changes\n│       │   └── components/     # QML UI components\n│       │       ├── Main.qml         # Root window: toast notifications, loader, hot-reload wiring\n│       │       ├── App.qml          # App layout: RowLayout with LeftPanel + RightPanel\n│       │       ├── generic/         # Reusable QML widgets\n│       │       │   ├── AppButton.qml\n│       │       │   ├── CustomImage.qml\n│       │       │   └── CustomRect.qml\n│       │       ├── left_panel/      # Agent list + session list\n│       │       │   ├── LeftPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── AgentRow.qml\n│       │       │   └── SessionRow.qml\n│       │       ├── right_panel/     # Chat area + input\n│       │       │   ├── RightPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── ChatPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── MessageBubble.qml\n│       │       │   ├── InputPanel.qml\n│       │       │   ├── InputField.qml\n│       │       │   ├── Attachment.qml\n│       │       │   └── AttachmentPreview.qml\n│       │       └── theme/\n│       │           ├── Theme.qml    # Singleton: Material You-ish color palette, spacing, font lists\n│       │           └── qmldir\n│       ├── logs/               # (empty directory, no files)\n│       ├── server/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   ├── server.py       # Server: wraps AsyncOpenAI, handles LLM + embedding requests (non-streaming and streaming)\n│       │   ├── models.py       # LLMPayload, LLMResponse, EmbeddingPayload/Response, OpenRouterUsage, LLMParams, etc.\n│       │   └── errors.py       # ServerRequestError, LLMRequestError, EmbeddingRequestError\n│       ├── toolkits/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   ├── registry.py     # ToolkitRegistry: manages core + registered + available kits, executes tools, generates schemas\n│       │   ├── builder.py      # build_tool(), build_toolkit(): construct Tool/ToolKit dataclasses from function blueprints\n│       │   ├── scanner.py      # scan_toolkit_dir(): walks kits/ dir, imports tools.py, reads SKILL.md, builds ToolKits\n│       │   ├── decorators.py   # @register_tool decorator: marks functions as tools for the scanner\n│       │   ├── models.py       # Tool, ToolKit, ToolBlueprint, ToolCall, ToolResult, ToolCallEvent, ToolResultEvent dataclasses\n│       │   ├── errors.py       # ToolKitError, ToolKitNotFoundError, ToolExecutionError\n│       │   └── kits/\n│       │       ├── file/       # Filesystem operations toolkit\n│       │       │   ├── SKILL.md    # Instruction document for filesystem tools (sandbox rules, conventions)\n│       │       │   └── tools.py    # read_file, read_document, write_file, append_file, make_dir, list_dir, move_file, copy_file, get_file_info, delete_file_or_dir\n│       │       └── git/        # Git operations toolkit\n│       │           ├── SKILL.md    # Instruction document for git tools (ordering, commit format, safety)\n│       │           └── tools.py    # git_status, git_add, git_commit, git_diff, git_restore\n│       └── utils/\n│           └── logger.py       # Logging setup: Rich console handler + rotating file handler\n└── tests/                      # (empty — no tests written)\n```\n\n## Installation and Setup\n\n1. **Clone the repository:**\n   ```bash\n   git clone <repo-url>\n   cd kagent\n   ```\n\n2. **Create a virtual environment** (Python ≥ 3.11):\n   ```bash\n   python -m venv .venv\n   source .venv/bin/activate   # Linux/Mac\n   # .venv\\Scripts\\activate    # Windows\n   ```\n\n3. **Install the package and dependencies:**\n   ```bash\n   pip install -e .\n   ```\n\n4. **Set up your API key:**\n   Create a `.env` file in the project root:\n   ```\n   API_KEY=sk-or-v1-your_openrouter_key_here\n   ```\n   (The app uses OpenRouter as its LLM provider. The base URL is hardcoded to `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1` in `gui/app.py`.)\n\n5. **Configure user settings (optional):**\n   Edit `saves/config.json` to change username, default agent, model, temperature, etc.\n\n6. **Run the application:**\n   ```bash\n   kagent\n   ```\n   Or directly:\n   ```bash\n   python -m modules.gui.app\n   ```\n\n## How to Use the System\n\n1. **Launch the app.** You\'ll see a dark-themed two-panel window. Left panel shows agents (with avatars) and their sessions. Right panel is the chat area.\n\n2. **Select an agent** from the left panel. Available agents: Amadeus, Ame, Aqua, Silver Wolf. Each has a unique personality defined in its Markdown file.\n\n3. **Create a new session** by clicking the "New Session" button (or similar) — sessions are scoped per agent. You can also click on an existing session to load its history.\n\n4. **Type your message** in the input field at the bottom right. Press **Enter** to send, **Shift+Enter** for a newline.\n\n5. **Attach images** (optional) by clicking the attachment button or dragging files into the input area. Images appear as thumbnails.\n\n6. **Watch the agent respond.** Status text indicates what\'s happening: "Thinking…" during LLM calls, "Running tool_name…" during tool execution.\n\n7. **Stop generation** at any time by clicking the stop button (appears while generating).\n\n8. **Right-click a session** in the left panel to rename or delete it.\n\n9. **Switch agents or sessions** freely — each agent has its own isolated conversation history.\n\n## OOP Implementation\n\n### Key Classes\n\n| Class | File | Role |\n|-------|------|------|\n| `ProgramError` | `errors.py` | Base exception for all project errors. Has a `message` field. |\n| `BaseAgent` (ABC) | `agents/models.py` | Abstract base for all agents. Owns name, model, system prompt, LLM params. Defines `generate()` and abstract `_build_payload()`. |\n| `BasicAgent` | `agents/models.py` | Stateless one-shot agent (system + user message, no history, no tools). Skips speaker tag, ignores username. Used for summarizers or one-off tasks. |\n| `CompleteAgent` | `agents/models.py` | Stateful agent with message history, tool calling, and a multi-loop run cycle (`_run_loop` up to `_max_loops`). The main agent type for chat. Has `run()` (yields events) and `generate()` (drains loop). |\n| `AgentDefinition` | `agents/models.py` | Pydantic model parsed from frontmatter: name, image_path, type (basic/complete), language_model, max_loop, params. |\n| `AgentError` | `agents/errors.py` | Subclass of ProgramError, adds a `name` field. |\n| `Database` | `database/database.py` | SQLite singleton (`@final` class, module-level `DATABASE` instance). CRUD for sessions, messages, attachments. Foreign keys with ON DELETE CASCADE. |\n| `SessionRow` / `MessageRow` / `MemoryRow` | `database/models.py` | Pydantic models for DB rows. `MessageRow` has `attachments: tuple[str, ...]`. `MemoryRow` is defined but never used. |\n| `Server` | `server/server.py` | Wraps `AsyncOpenAI` client. Methods: `send_request_llm()`, `send_request_embedding()`. Includes `_request_llm_streaming()` (unused). |\n| `ServerRequestError` / `LLMRequestError` / `EmbeddingRequestError` | `server/errors.py` | Exception hierarchy: `ServerRequestError → AgentError → ProgramError`. |\n| `ToolkitRegistry` | `toolkits/registry.py` | Manages three kit dicts: `_core_kits` (always active — includes the `registry` kit itself with `register_kit`/`list_kits`), `_registered_kits`, `_available_kits`. Generates `schemas` (OpenAI tool definitions), `skills` (concatenated instructions). Has `execute_tool()` for dispatching calls. |\n| `ToolKit` / `Tool` / `ToolBlueprint` / `ToolResult` | `toolkits/models.py` | Dataclasses. `ToolResult[T]` is generic with `ok`, `message`, `data`, `expose_data`, and `to_content()` (serializes to JSON string for the LLM). |\n| `ToolExecutionError` / `ToolKitError` / `ToolKitNotFoundError` | `toolkits/errors.py` | Exception hierarchy for toolkit errors, with `kit_name` and `tool_name` fields. |\n| `AppController` | `gui/controller.py` | `QObject` that bridges QML and Python. Holds references to backends via protocols. Emits signals: `selectedAgentChanged`, `selectedSessionChanged`, `generatingChanged`, `errorOccurred`, `restoreInput`. Manages async send tasks per session. |\n| `AgentListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` exposing agent names and image paths to QML ListView via custom roles. |\n| `SessionListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` for sessions with `reset_to()`, `prepend()`, `rename()`, `remove_by_id()`. |\n| `MessageListModel` | `gui/models.py` | `QAbstractListModel` for messages with pending message support (temporary IDs, `confirm_pending()`, `remove_by_id()`). |\n| `AttachmentListModel` | `gui/models.py` | Manages file attachments before sending. `take()` clears and returns, `restore()` puts back on failure. |\n| `CodeHighlighter` | `gui/highlighter.py` | `QObject` with `@pyqtSlot` methods. Applies Pygments styles to `QTextDocument` via `QTextCursor` mergeCharFormat. |\n| `QmlReloader` | `gui/loader.py` | Watches QML directory via `QFileSystemWatcher`, debounces changes with a 150ms `QTimer`, calls `engine.clearComponentCache()` then emits `reload`. |\n| `MockAgentsBackend` / `MockSessionBackend` | `backend.py` | Protocol implementations. `MockAgentsBackend` uses `scan_agent_dir()` and delegates to `CompleteAgent.run()`. `MockSessionBackend` wraps `Database`. |\n\n### Encapsulation\n\n- **`CompleteAgent._messages`** is private — history is only modified inside `_run_loop()` and `_record_failure()`. External code can only call `reset()`, `run()`, or `generate()`.\n- **`ToolkitRegistry`** encapsulates its three kit dicts and the `_tool_to_kit` lookup. External code interacts only through `register_kit()`, `list_kits()`, `execute_tool()`, and the read-only `schemas`/`skills`/`available_kits` properties.\n- **`Database`** is a `@final` class — all internal SQL is hidden behind session/message CRUD methods.\n- **`AppController`** encapsulates async task management (`_tasks` dict), per-session status tracking (`_status` dict), and all signal emissions.\n\n### Inheritance\n\n- **`ProgramError` → `AgentError`** (adds `name`), → **`DatabaseError`** (no additions), → **`ToolKitError`** (adds `kit_name`), → **`ToolExecutionError`** (adds `tool_name`), → **`ToolKitNotFoundError`**\n- **`AgentError` → `ServerRequestError`** → **`LLMRequestError`** / **`EmbeddingRequestError`**\n- **`BaseAgent`** (ABC) → **`BasicAgent`** (overrides `_build_user_message()`, `_build_payload()`)\n- **`BaseAgent`** → **`CompleteAgent`** (overrides `_build_payload()` with tool schemas, adds `run()`, `_run_loop()`, `_run_tools()`, `generate()` with `tool_choice` param, `reset()`, `_record_failure()`)\n- **`AgentDefinition`** uses Pydantic model validation with `@model_validator` to enforce constraints (basic agents can\'t have `max_loop` or `image_path`)\n- Custom `QAbstractListModel` subclasses: **`AgentListModel`**, **`SessionListModel`**, **`MessageListModel`**, **`AttachmentListModel`** — all override `rowCount()`, `data()`, `roleNames()`\n- **`AppController`** extends `QObject` (PyQt base for QML-visible objects)\n\n### Polymorphism\n\n- **Backend protocols:** `SessionsBackend` and `AgentsBackend` are `Protocol` classes in `backend.py`. `MockSessionBackend` and `MockAgentsBackend` implement them. `AppController` depends only on the protocol interfaces, not concrete classes.\n- **`BaseAgent.generate()`** is overridden in `CompleteAgent` with an overloaded signature (adds `tool_choice`, returns differently). Both subclasses satisfy the base contract.\n- **Agent events** are discriminated union types (`AgentEvent = GeneratingResponse | GenerationFinished | ToolCallStarted | ToolCallFinished | RunError`). `AppController._send()` dispatches via `match event:` pattern matching.\n- **Tool execution** in `ToolkitRegistry.execute_tool()` handles both async and sync functions transparently: async via `await`, sync via `loop.run_in_executor()`.\n- **`_build_user_message()`** is overridden: `BaseAgent` tags with `[User name]`, `BasicAgent` strips the tag and just uses plain text.\n- **Error handling in `CompleteAgent._run_tools()`** — tool failures never raise; they return `ToolResult(ok=False)` which the model can see and retry.\n\n## Database\n\n**File:** `data/agent.db` — SQLite3.\n\n### Table: `sessions`\n| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT | Unique session ID |\n| `title` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Session display name |\n| `agent_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Which agent this session belongs to |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMP | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Creation timestamp (UTC) |\n\n### Table: `messages`\n| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT | Unique message ID |\n| `session_id` | INTEGER | NOT NULL, FK → sessions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE | Parent session |\n| `speaker_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Who said it (username or agent name) |\n| `role` | TEXT | NOT NULL | "user" or "assistant" |\n| `text` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Message content |\n| `trace` | TEXT | nullable | (unused — never written to) |\n| `created_at` | TIMESTAMP | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Message timestamp (UTC) |\n\n### Table: `attachments`\n| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n| `id` | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT | Unique attachment ID |\n| `message_id` | INTEGER | NOT NULL, FK → messages(id) ON DELETE CASCADE | Parent message |\n| `path` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Filesystem path to the attachment |\n\n### Indexes\n- `idx_messages_session` on `messages(session_id, id)`\n- `idx_attachments_message` on `attachments(message_id)`\n\n### Major Database Operations\n\n| Operation | Function | SQL |\n|-----------|----------|-----|\n| **Create session** | `create_session(title, agent_name)` | `INSERT INTO sessions` |\n| **Read session** | `get_session(id)` | `SELECT * FROM sessions WHERE id = ?` |\n| **List sessions** | `get_session_list(agent_name)` | `SELECT * FROM sessions WHERE agent_name = ? ORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC` |\n| **Rename session** | `rename_session(title, id)` | `UPDATE sessions SET title = ? WHERE id = ?` |\n| **Delete session** | `delete_session(id)` | `DELETE FROM sessions WHERE id = ?` (cascades to messages and attachments) |\n| **Create message** | `add_message(session_id, role, text, speaker_name, attachments)` | `INSERT INTO messages` + `INSERT INTO attachments` (executemany) — wrapped in a transaction |\n| **Read messages** | `get_messages(session_id)` | `SELECT * FROM messages WHERE session_id = ? ORDER BY id` + `SELECT path FROM attachments JOIN messages ... WHERE session_id = ?` — grouped by message_id |\n| **Read single message** | `get_message(message_id)` | `SELECT * FROM messages WHERE id = ?` + `SELECT path FROM attachments WHERE message_id = ?` |\n\nUTC timestamps from SQLite are converted to local timezone 12-hour format (`"%b %d, %I:%M %p"`) via `_utc_to_local_12h()`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nFound in `docs/imgs/`:\n\n| File | Size | Description |\n|------|------|-------------|\n| `welcome_screen.png` | 63 KB | Initial state before any session is selected — shows the agent list in the left panel and a welcome/placeholder in the right panel |\n| `sample_chat1.png` | 185 KB | Example conversation with an agent showing user messages and agent responses |\n| `sample_chat2.png` | 236 KB | Another conversation example, possibly showing code blocks with syntax highlighting |\n| `session_rennaming.png` | 167 KB | Session rename dialog — shows right-click context menu or rename input field |\n| `vision_model.png` | 280 KB | Chat with an image attachment being processed by a vision-capable model — shows the image thumbnail in a message bubble |\n\n## Testing\n\n**The `tests/` directory exists but is completely empty.** No test files have been written. The project currently has zero automated tests.\n\n### Manual Testing Approach (what was likely done)\n\n- **Agent loading:** Launched app, verified all 4 agents appear in the left panel with correct avatars\n- **Session CRUD:** Created sessions, selected them, renamed via right-click dialog, deleted them\n- **Message sending:** Sent messages, verified they appear in the chat, waited for agent responses\n- **Tool calling:** Sent messages like "list files" or "create a file called test.txt" to trigger tool use\n- **Image attachments:** Attached images via the file picker, sent, verified thumbnails in message bubbles and that they appeared in the API request\n- **Stop generation:** Clicked the stop button mid-generation\n- **UI hot-reload:** Edited a QML file and verified the UI reloaded automatically\n\n### Code-level verification points (from reading the source)\n\n- Agent scanner (`agents/builder.py`) handles: missing definitions directory, missing global prompt, non-Markdown files, invalid YAML, invalid frontmatter params, unexpected exceptions — all with appropriate warnings/errors and graceful skip.\n- Database schema creation uses `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` + `CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS` — safe to re-run.\n- `Database.add_message()` wraps the INSERT + attachment inserts in a `with self.conn:` transaction block.\n- `CompleteAgent._run_loop()` catches `BaseException` (including `asyncio.CancelledError`) to always leave history consistent.\n- File tools validate paths against a sandbox root directory — blocked paths are unreachable even with `..` or symlinks.\n- `delete_file_or_dir` requires explicit two-step confirmation (no `confirm` → report only, `confirm=True` → trash it).\n\n## Known Issues / Limitations\n\n1. **No tests** — the `tests/` directory exists but is completely empty. Zero automated test coverage.\n2. **`trace` column unused** — `messages.trace` is defined in the schema but never written to by any code.\n3. **`config/models.py` is empty** — models intended for config validation were started but never populated.\n4. **`logs/` module directory is empty** — `src/modules/logs/` has no `__init__.py` and no files.\n5. **`MemoryRow` is dead code** — defined in `database/models.py` but nothing creates, reads, or writes to a `memories` table. No migration for it exists in the schema.\n6. **No remote git operations** — the git toolkit explicitly only supports status, add, commit, diff, restore. Push, pull, clone, fetch, branch, merge, rebase, log, reset, checkout are all blocked.\n7. **Hardcoded absolute path in config** — `saves/config.json` contains `"system_prompt_path": "/home/toffeezzz/Projects/python/cli-agent/SYSTEM_PROMPT.md"` which won\'t exist on other machines. This path is not actually used by the GUI code (agents get their system prompt from their definition files), but it\'s misleading.\n8. **Username hardcoded** — `AppController.__init__` sets `self._username = "toffeezzz"` — the username from `saves/config.json` is not read. All user messages are tagged `[User toffeezzz]`.\n9. **No streaming in the UI** — `Server._request_llm_streaming()` exists but is never called. The GUI awaits the full non-streaming response.\n10. **database file starts empty** — the `agent.db` symlink in the project root (if any) points to 0 bytes; the real database is in `data/agent.db` after first run.\n11. **No user authentication** — anyone who runs the app gets full access. Single-user only, no multi-user support.\n12. **Avatar for Ame uses `.jpg` extension but `image_path: "ame.jpg"`** — works fine since `AGENT_AVATAR_DIR / "ame.jpg"` exists.\n\n## Author\n\n**toffeezzz** — no section specified in source.', created_at='Oct 05, 06:51 AM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=())]) with args () and kwargs {} from queue
