2026-10-07 20:41:07 | INFO     | modules.agents.models:130 | Say: [Agent Amadeus] For a "hover to reveal more info" pattern—like a review preview card—the cleanest approach in QtQuick is **a local overlay controlled by `HoverHandler`**. You already have the building blocks in your codebase. Something like this: ```qml Item { id: card // The thing being hovered Rectangle { id: thumbnail width: 200; height: 200 color: "#E4E4E4" } // The hover-revealed card Rectangle { id: popover anchors.top: thumbnail.bottom anchors.left: thumbnail.left width: 300 height: 200 radius: 12 color: "white" // Shadow to lift it visually DropShadow { enabled: popover.visible } visible: hover.hovered Behavior on opacity { NumberAnimation { from: 0; to: 1 duration: 150 easing: Easing.InOutSine } } ColumnLayout { anchors.fill: parent anchors.margins: 16 Text { text: "★★★★☆" font.pixelSize: 16 color: root.accent } Text { text: "“Great stay, very clean room and friendly staff.”" font.pixelSize: 14 wrapMode: Text.WordWrap } Text { text: "— Alex, March 2025" font.pixelSize: 12 color: "#6B6B6B" } }... (+754 chars)
2026-10-07 20:41:07 | DEBUG    | modules.agents.models:136 | Say (full): [Agent Amadeus] For a "hover to reveal more info" pattern—like a review preview card—the cleanest approach in QtQuick is **a local overlay controlled by `HoverHandler`**. You already have the building blocks in your codebase.

Something like this:

```qml
Item {
  id: card

  // The thing being hovered
  Rectangle {
    id: thumbnail
    width: 200; height: 200
    color: "#E4E4E4"
  }

  // The hover-revealed card
  Rectangle {
    id: popover
    anchors.top: thumbnail.bottom
    anchors.left: thumbnail.left
    width: 300
    height: 200
    radius: 12
    color: "white"

    // Shadow to lift it visually
    DropShadow {
      enabled: popover.visible
    }

    visible: hover.hovered

    Behavior on opacity {
      NumberAnimation {
        from: 0; to: 1
        duration: 150
        easing: Easing.InOutSine
      }
    }

    ColumnLayout {
      anchors.fill: parent
      anchors.margins: 16

      Text {
        text: "★★★★☆"
        font.pixelSize: 16
        color: root.accent
      }

      Text {
        text: "“Great stay, very clean room and friendly staff.”"
        font.pixelSize: 14
        wrapMode: Text.WordWrap
      }

      Text {
        text: "— Alex, March 2025"
        font.pixelSize: 12
        color: "#6B6B6B"
      }
    }
  }

  HoverHandler {
    id: hover
  }
}
```

**Why this over other options:**

| Component | Problem |
|-----------|---------|
| `Popup` | Requires explicit open/close, doesn't track hover position naturally, feels modal |
| `Tooltip` | Only handles short text, no layout, no styling |
| `Loader` | Overkill for a small card, adds latency on hover |

**Your own `NavLink` already proves the pattern works** — `HoverHandler` + property binding + `Behavior` animation. Just scale it up to a full card layout.

---

If you want to get fancier (positioning relative to cursor, dismissing on leave), you can wrap it in a `Flickable`-like container with a `Timer` for a small delay before showing, but for a first pass the above is dead simple and fits your existing style.
