ageRow(id=98, session_id=10, role='assistant', text='Let me also peek into the subdirectories to get the full picture.', created_at='Oct 07, 10:50 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=99, session_id=10, role='assistant', text="Alright, here's the full picture of `src/modules/gui/`:\n\n---\n\n**Files (root of gui/):**\n\n| File | Size | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| `app.py` | 1.1 KB | Entry point — sets up the PyQt6 app, QML engine, wires the `Controller` and `QmlReloader` into QML context, loads `Main.qml` |\n| `controller.py` | 21 KB | The big one. `Controller` (QObject) — bridges Python backend to QML. Handles auth, room filters, search/booking, payments, reviews, and CRUD for tiers/rooms/users |\n| `models.py` | 10.6 KB | PyQt list models (`RoomListModel`, `ReviewListModel`, etc.) that expose Python data to QML via roles. Also has `RoomModel`/`ReviewModel` dataclasses, a `to_qt()` converter, and a generic `BaseListModel` |\n| `reloader.py` | 1.5 KB | `QmlReloader` — watches the `components/` directory for QML changes, clears the engine cache, and emits a reload signal. Dev workflow helper |\n\n**Subdirectories:**\n\n- **`components/`** — all the QML UI:\n  - `Main.qml` (364 B) — likely just loads `App.qml`\n  - `App.qml` (1.4 KB) — main app shell\n  - `auth_page/`, `home_page/`, `room_list_page/`, `reservation_page/`, `reservation_form/`, `generic/` — page-level QML components\n\n- **`images/`** — 8 image files:\n  - Room photos: `basic_room1.jpg`, `basic_room2.jpg`, `deluxe_room1.jpg`, `deluxe_room2.jpg`, `suite_room1.jpg`, `suite_room2.jpg`\n  - `home_bg.jpg` (3.5 MB) — likely the homepage background\n  - `header_logo.png` (35 KB) — logo\n\n- **`__pycache__/`** — ignore\n\n---\n\nIt's a PyQt6 + QML hotel booking app. The Python side handles all the logic and data, QML handles the UI. The `Controller` is the central bridge, the models convert data into something QML's list views can consume, and the reloader makes QML edits live without restarting.\n\nWhat's next? Want me to dive into any of the QML components, or head somewhere else in the codebase?", created_at='Oct 07, 10:50 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=100, session_id=10, role='user', text='did you read the qml? read them all if you didnt', created_at='Oct 07, 10:51 PM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=101, session_id=10, role='assistant', text='Fair point, I only listed the structure. Let me grab all the QML files now.\n\n', created_at='Oct 07, 10:51 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=102, session_id=10, role='assistant', text='Now let me read every QML file.', created_at='Oct 07, 10:51 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=103, session_id=10, role='assistant', text='Done, now I\'ve got the full picture of all the QML files. Here\'s a summary:\n\n---\n\n**`Main.qml`** — App entry point. Creates a 1200×800 window, loads `App.qml` via a Loader. Listens for a `reloader` signal to refresh the UI during development.\n\n**`App.qml`** — Root component. Manages page routing via `currentPage` property. Hosts all pages (HomePage, RoomListPage, ReservationListPage, ReservationForm, RegisterPage, LoginPage) and toggles visibility. Defines the accent color (`#E8B84F`).\n\n**Auth pages:**\n- **`LoginPage.qml`** — Email/password login form. Has a `PillButton` and `FormField` component. Resets on show. Calls `controller.login()`.\n- **`RegisterPage.qml`** — Registration form (name, email, phone, password, confirm). Validates email format, password length ≥ 8, and matching passwords. Calls `controller.register()`. Shows success state after registration.\n\n**Generic components:**\n- **`AccentButton.qml`** — Simple gold pill button with hover darkening.\n- **`CustomButton.qml`** — CustomRect + Text + MouseArea. A raw clickable rect.\n- **`CustomRect.qml`** — A rectangle with a debug border toggle.\n- **`Header.qml`** — Top navigation bar. Logo, page links (Home/Reservations/Rooms/About), login/signup or user name/logout depending on auth state.\n- **`NavLink.qml`** — A single nav link with an animated underline on active state.\n- **`RoomCard.qml`** — The big one. Room preview card with image, details, rating stars, and a hover overlay showing recent reviews and a "Book now" button. Has a `maxReviews: 3` constant and shows `reviews.slice(-maxReviews).reverse()`.\n- **`SearchField.qml`** — A label + value column used in the search bar.\n\n**Home page:**\n- **`HomePage.qml`** — Hero section with background image and overlay text, "Our rooms" grid using `controller.roomListModel`, footer.\n- **`SearchBar.qml`** — Search bar with check-in/out, guests, room type fields and a search button. Currently uses placeholder properties.\n\n**Reservation form:**\n- **`ReservationForm.qml`** — Full booking form. Room preview card, date inputs (YYYY-MM-DD), guest spinner, payment method selection (online/counter/later), cost summary, and confirm button. Calls `controller.bookRoom()` and optionally `controller.pay()`. Shows success state.\n\n**Reservation list:**\n- **`ReservationListPage.qml`** — Lists user\'s reservations with details, payment history, status badges. Uses `controller.reservationListModel`. Shows a RoomCard for each reservation.\n\n**Room list page:**\n- **`RoomListPage.qml`** — Room browsing with filters (dates, guests, price range), tier chips, and a responsive grid of RoomCards. Empty state messaging.\n\n---\n\nThat\'s all 16 QML files. The UI is structured, and the Python `Controller` powers most of the data binding. Anything specific you want to look into next?', created_at='Oct 07, 10:51 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=104, session_id=10, role='user', text='alright great thanks, what I need next is for you to make an about me page. make it still slick and modern UI. just place placeholders for now since Ill edit it myself. Just state the authors and what the app was made of like python, qml and stuff. there are two authors backend and frontend', created_at='Oct 07, 10:54 PM', speaker_name='toffeezzz', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=105, session_id=10, role='assistant', text='Let me check `App.qml` to see exactly how pages are wired in, so I can match the pattern.', created_at='Oct 07, 10:54 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=106, session_id=10, role='assistant', text='The Header already lists "About" in its nav — nice. Let me check the existing page styling to match the aesthetic.', created_at='Oct 07, 10:54 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=107, session_id=10, role='assistant', text='Perfect — the Header already links to "About", so it\'s just wiring up the page. Let me create it.\n\n', created_at='Oct 07, 10:54 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=108, session_id=10, role='assistant', text='Let me quickly check one of the existing pages to match the layout pattern exactly.', created_at='Oct 07, 10:54 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=109, session_id=10, role='assistant', text='Now let me create the About page and wire it into `App.qml`.', created_at='Oct 07, 10:55 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=110, session_id=10, role='assistant', text='Now wire it into `App.qml` — add the import and the page component:\n\n', created_at='Oct 07, 10:55 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=111, session_id=10, role='assistant', text='The Header already has "About" in its nav links, so we\'re golden. Let me verify the new page looks right:', created_at='Oct 07, 10:55 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=()), MessageRow(id=112, session_id=10, role='assistant', text='Done! Here\'s what I did:\n\n**Created** `src/modules/gui/components/about_page/AboutPage.qml` — a full about page with:\n\n- **Hero section** — light gray banner with "About this project" title and a brief subtitle\n- **Tech stack** — Python, PyQt 6, QML, SQLite listed with gold accent dots\n- **Features** — four feature bullet points with checkmarks\n- **Authors** — two side-by-side cards for Backend and Frontend developers, each with `[Author Name]` placeholders and a short description of their role. You can drop real names in there\n- **Footer** — matches the rest of the app\n\n**Wired** it into `App.qml` — added the import and the `AboutPage` component, visible when `currentPage === "About"`.\n\nThe Header already had "About" in its nav links, so it should show up in the top bar without any extra work. Give it a spin and let me know if you want anything tweaked!', created_at='Oct 07, 10:56 PM', speaker_name='Amadeus', attachments=())]) with args () and kwargs {} to thread worker queue
