e line into backend/API logic. Stop at the UI-State interface.\n\nPlease acknowledge that you understand these constraints and scope limits, then provide the **Step 1 Initial Reconnaissance list** based on the files you find in that dir\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Alright, I understand the constraints. Let me start with reconnaissance. First, I'll explore the directory structure."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Now let me read all the QML component files in the subdirectories.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Alright, I\'ve read every file in the tree. Here\'s the **Step 1 Reconnaissance List**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Major GUI Screens / Views\n\nEvery screen is a page managed by `App.qml`\'s `currentPage` router:\n\n| Screen | QML File | Route Name |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Home** | `home_page/HomePage.qml` | `"Home"` |\n| **Rooms** | `room_list_page/RoomListPage.qml` | `"Rooms"` |\n| **Reserve** (booking form) | `reservation_form/ReservationForm.qml` | `"Reserve"` |\n| **Reservations** (history) | `reservation_page/ReservationListPage.qml` | `"Reservations"` |\n| **Login** | `auth_page/LoginPage.qml` | `"Login"` |\n| **Register** | `auth_page/RegisterPage.qml` | `"Register"` |\n| **About** | `about_page/AboutPage.qml` | `"About"` |\n\nThe **Main.qml** (`Window` → `Loader` → `App.qml`) is the single entry point. `App.qml` owns page visibility switching via `currentPage`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. UI Components (Reusable & Inline)\n\n### Reusable / Shared Components (`generic/`)\n\n| Component | File | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Header** | `generic/Header.qml` | Top nav bar: logo, page links, login/signup/logout. Reads `controller.isLoggedIn` and `controller.currentUserName`. |\n| **NavLink** | `generic/NavLink.qml` | Single nav link with animated underline. Emits `clicked`. |\n| **AccentButton** | `generic/AccentButton.qml` | Gold rounded button. Emits `clicked`. |\n| **CustomButton** | `generic/CustomButton.qml` | Generic button base (text + font size). |\n| **CustomRect** | `generic/CustomRect.qml` | Debug rectangle with magenta border. |\n| **RoomCard** | `generic/RoomCard.qml` | Room preview card: image, info, hover overlay with star rating + recent reviews + "Book now" button. Emits `bookRequested(roomNumber)`. |\n| **SearchField** | `generic/SearchField.qml` | Label + value chip used inside search bars. Emits `clicked`. |\n\n### Page-Specific / Inline Components (defined inside their owning `.qml`)\n\n| Component | Defined In | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| **SearchBar** | `home_page/SearchBar.qml` | Horizontal bar: check-in, check-out, guests, room type, Search button. Emits `searchRequested`, `*Clicked` signals. |\n| **FilterChip** | `room_list_page/RoomListPage.qml` | Pill-shaped toggle chip for tier filter and Apply/Clear. |\n| **FilterField** | `room_list_page/RoomListPage.qml` | Labelled text field for date/price inputs. |\n| **PillButton** | `auth_page/LoginPage.qml`, `RegisterPage.qml`, `reservation_form/ReservationForm.qml` | Pill-shaped button (primary/secondary variant). |\n| **FormField** | `auth_page/LoginPage.qml`, `RegisterPage.qml`, `reservation_form/ReservationForm.qml` | Labelled text input with styled background. |\n| **SummaryRow** | `reservation_form/ReservationForm.qml` | Label-value row for the booking summary. |\n| **PaymentOption** | `reservation_form/ReservationForm.qml` | Selectable radio-style payment card (online / counter). |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Reactive Signals & State Triggers\n\n### A. UI Navigation Signals (QML-internal, no backend)\n\n| Signal | Source | Target |\n|---|---|---|\n| `navigateRequested(page)` | Every page | `App.qml` → switches `currentPage` |\n| `bookRequested(roomNum, dateIn, dateOut, guests)` | `RoomCard` → `RoomListPage` | Forwards to `ReservationForm.open(...)` + page switch |\n| `searchRequested` | `SearchBar` | (Prepared for future use) |\n| `checkInClicked`, `checkOutClicked`, `guestsClicked`, `roomTypeClicked` | `SearchBar` | (Prepared for future use) |\n| `reloader.onReload()` | `reloader.py` → `Main.qml` | Clears QML cache and reloads `App.qml` |\n\n### B. Controller Signals (PyQt `pyqtSignal` → QML `Connections`)\n\n| Signal | Emitted When | Listened By |\n|---|---|---|\n| `controller.currentUserChanged` | Login / logout / profile update / delete | `ReservationListPage.qml` re-fetches user reservations |\n\n### C. State Properties Read from Controller (drive UI visibility/labels)\n\n| Property | Used By |\n|---|---|\n| `controller.isLoggedIn` | Header (toggle login buttons vs. user name + logout), ReservationListPage (show list vs. prompt) |\n| `controller.currentUserName` / `currentUserEmail` | Header, ReservationForm (prefilled guest field) |\n| `controller.roomListModel` | HomePage (room preview grid), RoomListPage (filtered grid), ReservationForm (selected room card) |\n| `controller.roomTierListModel` | RoomListPage (tier filter chips) |\n| `controller.reservationListModel` | ReservationListPage (ListView of reservations) |\n| `controller.reviewListModel` | (Prepared, used via RoomCard\'s `reviews` role) |\n\n### D. Controller Slots (pyqtSlot — the "Signal Boundary" where QML fires into Python)\n\n**Auth & Profile:**\n- `controller.login(email, password)` → returns error string or "" + sets current user\n- `controller.register(fullname, email, phone, password)` → returns error string or "" + logs in\n- `controller.logout()`\n- `controller.changePassword(old, new)`\n- `controller.updateProfile(userId, fullname, email, phone)`\n- `controller.deleteUser(userId)`\n\n**Room Browsing & Filtering:**\n- `controller.refreshRooms(tierId)`\n- `controller.refreshTiers()`\n- `controller.setRoomFilters(tier, dateIn, dateOut, guests, minPrice, maxPrice)` → returns error string or ""\n- `controller.clearRoomFilters()`\n\n**Booking & Payments:**\n- `controller.bookRoom(userId, roomNum, dateIn, dateOut)` → returns error string or ""\n- `controller.cancelReservation(reservationNum)`\n- `controller.searchAvailableRooms(dateIn, dateOut, guests)`\n- `controller.clearAvailableRooms()`\n- `controller.pay(reservationNum, method, amount)`\n- `controller.payments(reservationNum)` → returns list\n- `controller.totalPaid(reservationNum)` / `controller.balanceDue(reservationNum)` → returns float\n- `controller.lastBookedReservation()` → returns int\n- `controller.roomDetails(roomNum)` → returns map\n\n**Reviews:**\n- `controller.addReview(userId, roomNum, rating, text)`\n- `controller.deleteReview(reviewId)`\n- `controller.refreshReviews(roomNum, userID)`\n\n**Admin (Room/Tier CRUD):**\n- `controller.addTier(name, basePrice)` / `deleteTier(tierId)`\n- `controller.addRoom(...)` / `setMaintenance(roomNum, on)` / `deleteRoom(roomNum)`\n\n**Data Refresh:**\n- `controller.refreshAll()`\n- `controller.refreshUsers()`\n- `controller.refreshReservations(userId)`\n\n---\n\nThat\'s the full inventory. The immediate "signal boundary" is every `pyqtSlot` call in `controller.py` — QML fires one of those, and control passes to the Python backend. The `pyqtSignal` named `currentUserChanged` is the only signal flowing *back* from Python to QML (aside from model-update notifications, which happen via Qt\'s model/view pattern through `BaseListModel`).\n\nIf this looks right, tell me to proceed and I\'ll write the full Typst document.'}]
